losure and reduce aspiration risk in patients with dysphagia.SHERKER EXERCISES:Shaker exercises are a specific type of exercise aimed at improving swallowing function in patients with dysphagia.CLINICAL TRIALS:Clinical trials are research studies that test the effectiveness of treatments, such as those for dysphagia in patients with head and neck cancer.SUPRA- AND INFRAHYOID MUSCLES:The supra- and infrahyoid muscles are groups of muscles in the neck that play a crucial role in swallowing and are targeted in dysphagia treatments.EXERCISES:Exercises are physical activities included in rehabilitation protocols to improve swallowing function in patients with dysphagia.NEUROMUSCULAR ELECTRICAL STIMULATION:Neuromuscular electrical stimulation is a technique used to enhance muscle activation in patients with swallowing difficulties.CHATTANOOGA GROUP:Chattanooga Group is the company that developed the VitalStim¬Æ device for treating dysphagia through neuromuscular electrical stimulation.EQUIPO PROFESIONAL:The professional team includes doctors, nurses, and speech therapists who monitor and provide guidance for patients with dysphagia.HIGIENE ORAL:Oral hygiene practices are essential for preventing respiratory infections in patients with dysphagia.EPILEPSIA:Epilepsia is a prominent medical journal dedicated to publishing research related to epilepsy and seizure disorders. It focuses on various aspects of epilepsy, including treatment approaches and dietary interventions, notably the ketogenic diet, which has been historically significant in managing the condition. The journal serves as a peer-reviewed platform for studies that explore the neurological manifestations of epilepsy, including its occurrence in specific patient populations, such as those with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes), where epilepsy contributes to their overall health challenges.

Epilepsy itself is a neurological disorder characterized by recurrent seizures, which can significantly impact treatment strategies for affected individuals, including those with conditions like oropharyngeal dysphagia. The condition is recognized in both English and Spanish literature, emphasizing its global relevance and the importance of dietary management, such as the ketogenic diet, among other treatment methods. Overall, Epilepsia plays a crucial role in advancing the understanding and treatment of epilepsy through rigorous research and scholarly discourse.ALIMENTACI√ìN ASISTIDA:Assisted feeding techniques are important for patients with dysphagia to ensure safe and effective nutrition.DIFICULTADES COGNITIVAS:Cognitive difficulties can impact a patient's ability to follow swallowing instructions and manage dysphagia.TUMOR ACTIVO:LANGMORE SE:Langmore SE is an author who contributed to the literature on the efficacy of exercises to rehabilitate dysphagia.PISENGA JM:Pisegna JM is an author who co-wrote a critique of the literature on dysphagia rehabilitation.HEGLAND KW:Hegland KW is an author who discussed nonsurgical treatment for swallowing rehabilitation.MURRY T:Murry T is an author who contributed to the discussion on nonsurgical treatment for swallowing rehabilitation.ROGUS-PULIA N:Rogus-Pulia N is a researcher who specializes in swallowing studies and has made significant contributions to the field of dysphagia rehabilitation. As an author, Rogus-Pulia N has focused on developing and promoting rehabilitation approaches specifically tailored for post-stroke patients experiencing difficulties with swallowing.ROBBINS J:Robbins J is an author who co-wrote on rehabilitation approaches for dysphagia.SUTTRUP I:Suttrup I is an author who studied dysphagia in Parkinson's Disease.NEWMAN R:Newman R is an author who wrote about the effect of bolus viscosity on swallowing safety and efficacy.VILARDELL N:Vilardell N is an author who co-wrote on bolus viscosity and swallowing.SPEYER R:Speyer R is an author who co-wrote on the effect of bolus viscosity on swallowing.LOGEMANN JA:Logemann JA is a prominent researcher and author recognized for her significant contributions to the field of swallowing disorders and interventions. She has extensively studied the treatment of oral and pharyngeal dysphagia, providing valuable insights and advancements in the management of these conditions. Her work has had a substantial impact on both clinical practices and academic research related to swallowing difficulties.ANDERSEN UT:Andersen UT is an author who reviewed texture modified foods for dysphagia.KJAERSGAARD A:Kjaersgaard A is an author who contributed to the review of texture modified foods.HANSEN T:Hansen T is an author who contributed to the review of texture modified foods.POULSEN I:Poulsen I is an author who contributed to the review of texture modified foods.YOUNG JL:Young JL is an author who studied the sequence of swallowing events.MACRAE P:Macrae P is an author who co-wrote on the sequence of swallowing events.ANDERSON C:Anderson C is an author who co-wrote on the sequence of swallowing events.TAYLOR-KAMARA I:Taylor-Kamara I is an author who co-wrote on the sequence of swallowing events.HUMBERT IA:Humbert IA is an author who co-wrote on the sequence of swallowing events.SHANAHAN TK:Shanahan TK is an author who studied the effect of chin-down posture on aspiration in dysphagic patients.PAULOSKI BR:Pauloski BR is a researcher and author known for their contributions to the field of swallowing disorders, particularly in cancer patients. They studied the effects of enhanced bolus flavors on oropharyngeal swallow, aiming to improve the swallowing experience for individuals undergoing treatment. Additionally, Pauloski BR co-wrote a publication that examined the effects of chin-down posture on aspiration, further highlighting their expertise in the dynamics of swallowing and aspiration risk management.RADEMAKER AW:Rademaker AW is a researcher and author known for significant contributions to the field of swallowing, particularly in patients who have undergone treatment for head and neck cancer. Rademaker AW has co-authored studies that explore the effects of chin-down posture on aspiration, furthering the understanding of swallowing mechanics and rehabilitation in this patient population.KAHRILAS PJ:Kahrilas PJ is an author who co-wrote on chin-down posture effects on aspiration.LEIGH JH:Leigh JH is an author who studied the influence of chin-down and chin-tuck maneuvers on swallowing kinematics.OH BM:Oh BM is an author who co-wrote on the influence of chin-down and chin-tuck maneuvers.SEO HG:Seo HG is an author who co-wrote on the influence of chin-down and chin-tuck maneuvers.LEE GJ:Lee GJ is an author who co-wrote on the influence of chin-down and chin-tuck maneuvers.MIN Y:Min Y is an author who co-wrote on the influence of chin-down and chin-tuck maneuvers.KIM K:Kim K is an author who co-wrote on the influence of chin-down and chin-tuck maneuvers.MANUAL DE DISFAGIA OROFAR("ENTITY":ANN REHABIL MED:Ann Rehabil Med is a medical journal that publishes research related to rehabilitation medicine, including studies on swallowing disorders.HEAD NECK:Head & Neck is a medical journal dedicated to the study and research of head and neck cancers and their treatment. It emphasizes the impact of these conditions on various aspects of patient health, particularly focusing on swallowing issues that arise in cancer patients. The journal covers a wide range of topics related to head and neck surgery and oncology, providing valuable insights into the challenges and advancements in the field.CODAS:Codas is a journal that publishes articles on communication disorders, including studies on swallowing and dysphagia.ARQ GASTROENTEROL:Arq Gastroenterol is a journal that publishes research related to gastroenterology, including studies on swallowing and dysphagia.CURRENT OPINION OTOLARYNGOL HEAD NECK SURG:Current Opinion in Otolaryngology and Head and Neck Surgery is a journal that discusses current trends and research in otolaryngology, including swallowing disorders.FOLIA PHONIATR LOGOP:Folia Phoniatrica et Logopaedica is a journal that publishes research on speech and language pathology, including studies on swallowing.J SPEECH LANG HEAR RES:Journal of Speech, Language, and Hearing Research is a journal that publishes research on communication disorders, including swallowing issues.AM J SPEECH LANG PATHOL:American Journal of Speech-Language Pathology is a journal that publishes research on speech and language disorders, including dysphagia.ARCH PHYS MED REHABIL:Archives of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation is a journal that publishes research on rehabilitation, including studies on swallowing therapies.IOWA ORAL PERFORMANCE INSTRUMENT:The Iowa Oral Performance Instrument (IOPI) is a specialized device designed for diagnosing and training the strength and endurance of the tongue and lips, particularly in patients with swallowing disorders. It is utilized to measure both tongue and hand strength and endurance, making it relevant in various studies related to dysphagia. The IOPI serves as a valuable tool in dysphagia research, aiding in the assessment and treatment of individuals experiencing difficulties with swallowing.RYU JS:Ryu JS is a researcher involved in the study of pharyngeal pressure events using high-resolution manometry.SONG SH:Song SH is a researcher who co-authored the study on head rotation and head tilt effects on swallowing.KOO JH:Koo JH is a researcher who contributed to the study on pharyngeal pressure events.LEE KD:Lee KD is a researcher involved in the study of swallowing mechanics.PARK HS:Park HS is a researcher who co-authored the study on the effects of head rotation and tilt on swallowing.LUNDY D:Lundy D is a researcher involved in the study of swallowing in head and neck cancer patients.SULLIVAN PA:Sullivan PA is a researcher who studied the effects of bolus flavors on swallowing.NEWMAN LA:Newman LA is a researcher who contributed to the study on oropharyngeal swallow in cancer patients.GATTO AR:Gatto AR is a researcher who studied the effects of sour taste and cold temperature on swallowing in stroke patients.COLA PC:Cola PC is a researcher involved in studies on swallowing and its mechanics.SILVA RG:Silva RG is a researcher who co-authored studies on swallowing in stroke patients.SPADOTTO AA:Spadotto AA is a researcher who studied the effects of temperature and taste on swallowing.RIBEIRO PW:Ribeiro PW is a researcher involved in swallowing studies related to stroke.SCHELP AO:Schelp AO is a researcher who contributed to studies on swallowing mechanics.HENRY MA:Henry MA is a researcher involved in studies on swallowing and its physiological aspects.REGAN J:Regan J is a researcher who studied the effects of thermal-tactile stimulation on swallowing in Parkinson's disease.WALSHE M:Walshe M is a researcher involved in swallowing studies related to Parkinson's disease.TOBIN WO:Tobin WO is a researcher who studied the timing of swallow in idiopathic Parkinson's disease.ROFES L:Rofes L is a researcher who studied the effects of natural capsaicinoids on swallowing response in older patients.MARTIN A:Martin A is a researcher who contributed to studies on swallowing in older patients.CRARY MA:Crary MA is a researcher known for their work in the field of swallowing disorders, particularly focusing on the adoption of therapies to manage these conditions. Additionally, Crary MA is recognized as one of the authors of the Functional Oral Intake Scale, which is specifically designed for assessing dysphagia in stroke patients. This scale plays a crucial role in evaluating and guiding the treatment of individuals with swallowing difficulties.CARNABY GD:Carnaby GD is a researcher involved in swallowing rehabilitation studies.LAZARUS C:Lazarus C is a researcher who studied the effects of maneuvers on swallowing function.CHAUDHURI G:Chaudhuri G is a researcher who studied cardiovascular effects of swallowing maneuvers in stroke patients.HILDNER CD:Hildner CD is a researcher involved in swallowing studies related to stroke.BRADY S:Brady S is a researcher who studied swallowing maneuvers in stroke patients.HUTCHINS B:Hutchins B is a researcher involved in swallowing studies.ALIGA N:Aliga N is a researcher who contributed to studies on swallowing maneuvers.ABADILLA E:Abadilla E is a researcher involved in swallowing studies.WHEELER-HEGLAND KM:Wheeler-Hegland KM is a researcher who studied submental sEMG and hyoid movement during swallowing maneuvers.ROSENBEK JC:Rosenbek JC is a researcher involved in swallowing studies.SAPIENZA CM:Sapienza CM is a researcher who studied swallowing maneuvers and their effects.FUKUOKA T:Fukuoka T is a researcher who studied the effects of effortful swallow and Mendelsohn maneuver on tongue pressure.ONO T:Ono T is a researcher involved in swallowing studies.HORI K:Hori K is a researcher who studied swallowing biomechanics.TAMINE K:Tamine K is a researcher involved in swallowing studies.NOZAKI S:Nozaki S is a researcher who studied swallowing mechanics.SHIMADA K:Shimada K is a researcher involved in swallowing studies.YAMAMOTO N:Yamamoto N is a researcher who studied swallowing mechanics.FUKUDA Y:Fukuda Y is a researcher involved in swallowing studies.DOMEN K:Domen K is a researcher who studied swallowing mechanics.LENIUS K:Lenius K is a researcher who studied the effects of lingual effort on swallow pressures.STIERWALT J:Stierwalt J is a researcher involved in swallowing studies.LAPOINTE LL:LaPointe LL is a researcher who studied swallowing mechanics.BOURGEOIS M:Bourgeois M is a researcher involved in swallowing studies.CARNABY G:Carnaby G is a researcher who studied swallowing rehabilitation.CRARY M:Crary M is a researcher involved in swallowing studies.ADAMS V:Adams V is a researcher who conducted a systematic review on tongue and hand strength in swallowing.MATHISEN B:Mathisen B is a researcher involved in swallowing studies.BAINES S:Baines S is a researcher who studied swallowing mechanics.CALLISTER R:Callister R is a researcher involved in swallowing studies.RUSCHE N:Rusche N is a researcher who studied swallowing mechanics.HIND JA:Hind JA is a researcher involved in swallowing studies.J AM GERIATR SOC:The Journal of the American Geriatrics Society (J AM GERIATR SOC) is a prominent publication that focuses on research related to aging and health issues affecting older adults. It publishes a variety of studies, including those examining the relationship between testosterone levels and frailty in older men, as well as research on dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. Through its diverse range of articles, the journal aims to advance the understanding of geriatric health and improve the quality of care for the aging population.J PHYS THER SCI:The Journal of Physical Therapy Science publishes research on physical therapy practices, including studies on swallowing therapies.OTOLARYNGOL HEAD NECK SURG:Otolaryngology - Head and Neck Surgery is a journal that publishes research on conditions affecting the ear, nose, throat, and related structures, including dysphagia.AM J PHYS MED REHABIL:The American Journal of Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation publishes research on rehabilitation practices, including studies on dysphagia in stroke patients.CLIN REHABIL:Clinical Rehabilitation is a journal that publishes research on rehabilitation practices, including studies on dysphagia and related therapies.RESEARCH GROUP FOR ASPIRATION PNEUMONIA:The Research Group for Aspiration Pneumonia is a collective focused on studying aspiration pneumonia, particularly in the elderly and its relation to dysphagia.PETERS K:Peters K is a researcher involved in studies on dysphagia and rehabilitation techniques.EROGLU ST:Eroglu ST is a researcher who has worked on neuromuscular electrical stimulation for dysphagia in stroke patients.PERLESS-CARR