 neck cancer.GOODWIN N:Goodwin N is a researcher contributing to studies on dysphagia and its treatments.CASH E:Cash E is a researcher involved in studies related to dysphagia.BHATT G:Bhatt G is a researcher who has worked on studies related to dysphagia treatments.SILVERMAN CL:Silverman CL is a researcher contributing to studies on dysphagia and rehabilitation.SPANOS WJ:Spanos WJ is a researcher involved in studies on dysphagia and its treatments.)<|COMPLETE|>UFDOF:The Functional Unit of Oropharyngeal Dysphagia (UFDOF), also known as Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar√≠ngea, is a specialized unit located within HUPA (Hospital Universitario Pr√≠ncipe de Asturias) in the Community of Madrid. This unit is dedicated to the evaluation, diagnosis, and treatment of patients suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. In addition to providing direct patient care, UFDOF is committed to training healthcare professionals to enhance the quality of care for individuals with dysphagia. Through its focused approach, UFDOF aims to improve the management of swallowing disorders and ensure comprehensive support for affected patients.JAPANESE SOCIETY OF DYSPHAGIA REHABILITATION:The Japanese Society of Dysphagia Rehabilitation (JSDR) is an organization that advocates for a transdisciplinary approach in the rehabilitation of dysphagia.LOGOPEDIA:Logopedia refers to the field of speech therapy that encompasses services aimed at the treatment of dysphagia, a condition that affects an individual's ability to swallow. It plays a crucial role in the rehabilitation of patients suffering from this disorder, providing essential support and therapeutic interventions to improve their swallowing capabilities and overall communication skills.TERAPIA OCUPACIONAL:Terapia Ocupacional (Occupational Therapy) is a discipline that plays a significant role in the rehabilitation of patients with dysphagia. The Terapia Ocupacional service specifically focuses on assisting these patients in their recovery process, utilizing various therapeutic techniques to improve their swallowing abilities and overall quality of life.ENFERMER√çA:Enfermer√≠a (Nursing) provides essential support in the care of patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects the ability to swallow. The nursing staff plays a crucial role in assessing patients and implementing dietary modifications as part of the treatment for swallowing disorders. Specifically, the nursing team is instrumental in the assessment and care of patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia within the hospital setting. Their expertise and interventions are vital for ensuring the well-being and recovery of these patients.NEUR√ìLOGOS:Neur√≥logos (Neurologists) are specialists involved in the assessment and treatment of dysphagia-related conditions.DIETISTAS AMERICANAS:Dietistas Americanas, or American Dietitians, are professionals who offer dietary advice and support specifically for patients experiencing dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing.EQUIPO INTERDISCIPLINAR:An interdisciplinary team is a group of professionals from various disciplines working together to address a specific patient situation in dysphagia treatment.EQUIPO MULTIDISCIPLINAR:The "EQUIPO MULTIDISCIPLINAR" is a multidisciplinary team composed of various healthcare professionals, including a psychiatrist, psychologist, endocrinologist, diabetes educator, dietitian/nutritionist, and social worker. This team collaborates to manage treatment priorities for patients with diabetes and eating disorders, ensuring comprehensive care tailored to individual needs. Additionally, the team includes professionals from different specialties who work together to provide care for patients with dysphagia and those requiring home parenteral nutrition. Furthermore, the team is involved in designing appropriate diets for patients in the context of renal insufficiency, highlighting their commitment to addressing diverse health challenges through a collaborative approach.EQUIPO TRANSDISCIPLINAR:A transdisciplinary team goes beyond traditional roles, allowing professionals to take on tasks from other disciplines to enhance patient care in dysphagia.ATENCI√ìN INTEGRAL:Atenci√≥n integral refers to the comprehensive care approach provided to patients with dysphagia, involving multiple disciplines.PROFESIONALES DE LA SALUD:"PROFESIONALES DE LA SALUD" refers to healthcare professionals who play a crucial role in providing medical services and support to patients. They are essential for the diagnosis and treatment of various conditions, including oropharyngeal dysphagia. These professionals are specifically involved in the treatment and rehabilitation of patients suffering from dysphagia, ensuring that individuals receive the necessary care and support to manage their condition effectively.ABORDAJE DE LA DISFAGIA:Abordaje de la disfagia refers to the strategies and methods used to treat and manage dysphagia.INTERVENCI√ìN CONJUNTA:Intervenci√≥n conjunta refers to the collaborative approach taken by various professionals in treating dysphagia.EVALUACI√ìN DE PATOLOG√çAS:Evaluaci√≥n de patolog√≠as refers to the assessment of medical conditions, including dysphagia, by a team of specialists.ENFOQUE MULTIDISCIPLINARIO:Enfoque multidisciplinario refers to the collaborative method involving multiple disciplines to address dysphagia treatment.VISI√ìN COMPLETA:Visi√≥n completa refers to the comprehensive perspective gained through a multidisciplinary approach in dysphagia care.)<|COMPLETE|>NEUROLOG√çA:The entity "NEUROLOG√çA" refers to a specialized unit within a hospital dedicated to the diagnosis and treatment of disorders related to the nervous system. This department plays a crucial role in addressing various neurological conditions, including those that may lead to complications such as dysphagia, which is difficulty in swallowing. Through its comprehensive approach, the Neurology department aims to manage and treat the underlying causes of these disorders effectively.MEDICINA INTERNA:The "MEDICINA INTERNA" refers to the Internal Medicine department, which is a medical specialty focused on the diagnosis, treatment, and prevention of diseases in adults. This specialty encompasses a wide range of conditions affecting multiple systems of the body. The department is particularly noted for its role in managing patients with dysphagia, ensuring coordinated care for these individuals. Additionally, the Internal Medicine department emphasizes dietary considerations as part of its comprehensive care approach for adult patients. Overall, "MEDICINA INTERNA" plays a crucial role in providing thorough medical attention and support for various adult health issues.ONCOLOG√çA:The Oncology department addresses dysphagia in patients with cancer-related complications.ENDOCRINOLOG√çA Y NUTRICI√ìN:"ENDOCRINOLOG√çA Y NUTRICI√ìN" is a specialized field of medicine that focuses on hormonal and nutritional health. It encompasses both clinical practice and research, as evidenced by the existence of a scientific journal dedicated to this discipline. The journal, also named "Endocrinolog√≠a y Nutrici√≥n," serves as a platform for disseminating research findings related to endocrinology and nutrition. 

In clinical settings, the Endocrinology and Nutrition department plays a crucial role in patient care, particularly for individuals with diabetes and those requiring nutritional support, such as dysphagia patients. This department is where patients are referred for evaluation after experiencing significant weight loss, highlighting its importance in managing various health concerns related to nutrition and hormonal balance.

Mart√≠n L√≥pez de la Torre Casares is noted for his specialization in this field, contributing to both the clinical and editorial aspects of endocrinology and nutrition. As an associate editor of the journal, he is involved in advancing knowledge and research in this vital area of healthcare.LOGOPEDAS:Logopedas are professionals who specialize in the evaluation and treatment of swallowing disorders, particularly in patients with dysphagia. They play a crucial role in assessing deglutition and the risk of aspiration in individuals receiving enteral nutrition. In both the United States and Europe, logopedas are primarily responsible for the care of patients with dysphagia, ensuring that these individuals receive appropriate interventions to manage their swallowing difficulties effectively.UNCYD:The Unidad de Nutrici√≥n Cl√≠nica y Diet√©tica (UNCyD) is a clinical nutrition unit dedicated to conducting nutritional assessments and screenings, particularly for patients over the age of 65. It operates within a team-oriented framework, offering nutritional support tailored to individuals with special needs. UNCyD focuses on the management of clinical nutrition and dietary practices to enhance patient care and well-being.COMUNIDAD DE MADRID:The Community of Madrid is an autonomous community in Spain that serves as a significant healthcare hub. It is home to the Hospital Universitario Pr√≠ncipe de Asturias (HUPA), which acts as a reference center for the treatment of patients suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia. Additionally, the region is notable for its specific measurement and reporting of congenital hypothyroidism incidence, highlighting its commitment to monitoring and addressing health issues within the population. Overall, the Community of Madrid plays a crucial role in providing specialized medical services and healthcare resources to its residents.EQUIPO DE DIRECCI√ìN:The Equipo de Direcci√≥n is the management team at the Hospital Universitario Pr√≠ncipe de Asturias responsible for overseeing the implementation of new healthcare initiatives.PROFESIONALES SANITARIOS:Healthcare professionals involved in the management of patients with DOF, including nurses, dietitians, speech therapists, and medical specialists.T√âCNICOS EN ALIMENTACI√ìN Y DIET√âTICA:Dietitians and nutrition technicians who assist in the dietary management of patients with dysphagia.M√âDICOS ESPECIALISTAS EN ENDOCRINOLOG√çA Y NUTRICI√ìN:Medical specialists in endocrinology and nutrition who provide care for patients with dysphagia.ESPECIALISTAS EN OTORRINOLARINGOLOG√çA:Otolaryngology specialists who are involved in diagnosing and treating swallowing disorders.ESPECIALISTAS EN REHABILITACI√ìN:Rehabilitation specialists who assist in the recovery and management of patients with dysphagia.FAR√çNGEA:FAR√çNGEA is an organization focused on multidisciplinary solutions in the Community of Madrid, dedicated to the professional development of its personnel.HUPA:HUPA is a healthcare center dedicated to the eradication of dysphagia and malnutrition, with a strong commitment to enhancing patient care through multidisciplinary approaches. Located in the Community of Madrid, HUPA oversees the Functional Unit of Orofar√≠ngea Dysphagia, offering specialized care for patients suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia. The institution emphasizes comprehensive and quality treatment, ensuring that patients receive thorough evaluation and management of their swallowing disorders. In addition to its focus on dysphagia, HUPA provides a range of medical services aimed at improving overall patient health and well-being.ALCAL√Å DE HENARES:Alcal√° de Henares is the head city of the Community of Madrid where the Functional Unit of Orofar√≠ngea Dysphagia is located.COMUNIDAD AUT√ìNOMA DE MADRID:The Community of Madrid is the autonomous community where the UFDOF operates, providing healthcare services to its population.CALIDAD ASISTENCIAL:Calidad asistencial refers to the quality of care provided to patients, encompassing various dimensions such as accessibility, equity, and effectiveness. It is particularly relevant in the context of managing specific conditions, such as dysphagia. Additionally, calidad asistencial represents the standard of care that the UFDOF aims to provide to its patients, ensuring that all aspects of patient care meet high-quality benchmarks.INNOVACI√ìN:Innovaci√≥n refers to the commitment of the UFDOF to incorporate innovative practices in the treatment of dysphagia.INVESTIGACI√ìN:Investigaci√≥n refers to the research efforts that the UFDOF is committed to in order to improve dysphagia treatment. Additionally, it encompasses the study of artificial home nutrition, which is necessary to determine its impact on quality of life and the early detection of mood disorders. This comprehensive approach highlights the importance of research in both enhancing treatment methods and understanding the broader implications of nutritional interventions on health and well-being.DOCENCIA:Docencia refers to the educational activities that the UFDOF engages in to train healthcare professionals.OTORRINOLARINGOLOGY:The Otorrinolaringolog√≠a service at HUPA specializes in ear, nose, and throat conditions, contributing to the multidisciplinary approach to dysphagia.REHABILITATION:Rehabilitation refers to the process of restoring health and functional ability in patients with chronic diseases through various therapeutic interventions, including nutritional support. The Rehabilitation service at HUPA specifically focuses on the recovery and rehabilitation of patients, including those who experience dysphagia, ensuring a comprehensive approach to patient care and recovery.NUTRITION CLINICAL AND DIETETICS:The Nutrition Clinical and Dietetics service at HUPA provides dietary support and nutritional care for patients, particularly those with dysphagia.HOSPITAL KITCHEN SERVICE:The Hospital Kitchen Service at HUPA prepares meals tailored to the needs of patients, including those with dysphagia.LOGOPEDIST:A logopedist at HUPA specializes in speech and language therapy, playing a crucial role in the care of patients with dysphagia.NURSES:Nurses at HUPA are trained in Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics, providing essential care for patients with dysphagia.COOKS:Cooks at HUPA prepare meals that meet the dietary needs of patients, including those with dysphagia.UNIT OF OROPHARYNGEAL DYSPHAGIA:The Unit of Oropharyngeal Dysphagia at HUPA is dedicated to providing multidisciplinary care for patients with swallowing difficulties.SERVICIO DE ORL:The Servicio de ORL (Otorhinolaryngology Service) at HUPA is dedicated to the diagnosis and treatment of conditions affecting the ear, nose, and throat. This includes a focus on swallowing disorders, specifically dysphagia. The service provides specialized care and assessments for patients with these conditions and collaborates with the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar√≠ngea to enhance patient outcomes. Through its comprehensive approach, the Servicio de ORL ensures that patients receive targeted and effective treatment for their otorhinolaryngological needs.SERVICIO DE REHABILITACI√ìN:The Rehabilitation Service at HUPA provides therapeutic interventions for patients recovering from various conditions, including swallowing difficulties.SERVICIO DE COCINA HOSPITALARIA:The Servicio de Cocina Hospitalaria at HUPA is dedicated to preparing and providing meals that are specifically tailored to meet the dietary needs of patients. This includes accommodating individuals undergoing swallowing assessments and ensuring that all meals align with the individualized diets prescribed by the UNCyD team. The service focuses on delivering nutrition that supports the health and recovery of patients, taking into account their unique nutritional requirements.CATALU√ëA:Catalu√±a is an autonomous community in Spain known for its comprehensive approach to public health and nutrition. In this region, administrative tools are available for hiring dietitians within the public health system, ensuring that nutritional needs are adequately addressed. Additionally, Catalu√±a has been the site of significant research, including studies on iron deficiency and overload among the adult population, highlighting its commitment to understanding and improving health outcomes. For patients requiring ongoing nutritional treatment, it is necessary to submit a justification report to the relevant primary care center, which underscores the region's structured approach to healthcare management. Furthermore, the dispensing of nutritional and dietary products, referred to as NED products, is facilitated through hospital pharmacies, and there are established agreements with the pharmaceutical industry to enable home delivery, enhancing accessibility for patients in need.VIDEOFUOROSCOPIA DE LA DEGLUCI√ìN:Videofluoroscopy of swallowing is a diagnostic test performed to evaluate swallowing disorders, conducted in the UFDOF unit.ALIMENTOS S√ìLIDOS:Solid foods of various textures are prepared for patients undergoing swallowing assessments at HUPA.MATERIAL PARA REALIZAR LOS TEST DE VOLUMEN-VISCOSIDAD:Materials for conducting volume-viscosity tests are used in the assessment of swallowing disorders at HUPA.NAVARRA:Navarra is an autonomous community in Spain known for its distinct characteristics and health statistics. It is notable for having one of the lowest mortality rates for Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) among women, indicating a relatively favorable health outcome in this demographic. Additionally, in Navarra, patients are required to submit a justification report to continue receiving treatment for their nutritional needs, reflecting the region's structured approach to healthcare management and patient support.NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL TOTAL:NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL TOTAL, also known as Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN), is a medical treatment that provides 100% of a patient's nutritional requirements through intravenous administration. This method is utilized when enteral nutrition is contraindicated or not tolerated, allowing nutrients to be delivered directly into the bloodstream, thereby bypassing the gastrointestinal tract. TPN is particularly important for patients who are unable to eat by mouth, ensuring they receive essential nutrients for their health and recovery.

In specific cases, such as when a patient loses their nasoenteric tube, TPN may be initiated to support their nutritional needs until they can resume oral feeding. This treatment serves as a critical intervention during hospitalization, ensuring that patients receive adequate nutritional support when traditional feeding methods are not viable. Overall, NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL TOTAL is a vital component of patient care for those requiring specialized nutritional support.EVALUACI√ìN NUTRICIONAL:EVALUACI√ìN NUTRICIONAL refers to the process of determining an individual's nutritional status through various measurements and analyses. This comprehensive evaluation is crucial for identifying dietary needs and nutritional support requirements, particularly for patients. It involves assessing a patient's dietary intake and overall nutritional status to ensure appropriate care is provided. This process is especially significant for individuals diagnosed with gastrointestinal cancers, as their nutritional needs may be more complex and require tailored interventions.ELECTROESTIMULACI√ìN:Electrostimulation is a therapeutic technique used in the rehabilitation of swallowing disorders.TOXINA BOTUL√çNICA:Botulinum toxin, commonly known as "TOXINA BOTUL√çNICA," is utilized in specific medical applications to address various health issues. It is employed in the treatment of bowel function disorders, helping to manage conditions that affect gastrointestinal motility. Additionally, botulinum toxin is used in targeted therapies for oropharyngeal dysphagia, a condition that impairs swallowing function, thereby improving the ability to swallow in affected individuals.MIOTOM√çA DEL CRICOFAR√çNGEO:Cricopharyngeal myotomy is a surgical procedure aimed at improving swallowing by cutting the muscle at the top of the esophagus.HISTORIA CL√çNICA:HISTORIA CL√çNICA refers to the comprehensive medical history of a patient, which is essential for assessing and treating various health conditions, including dysphagia and diarrhea. It encompasses a detailed record of the patient's medical background, including dietary history and other relevant health information. The historia cl√≠nica serves as a crucial document that not only tracks all follow-ups and treatments but also records the patient's health history and their responses to treatments. This medical record is fundamental for nutritional assessment and plays a vital role in guiding healthcare decisions related to the patient's treatment.VALORACI√ìN FUNCIONAL:Functional assessment involves evaluating a patient's physical capabilities, which is important in the context of dysphagia treatment.MEN√öS ALIMENTARIOS:Dietary menus are tailored food plans designed for patients with dysphagia, ensuring safe and appropriate food textures.SUPLEMENTOS ORALES:"SUPLEMENTOS ORALES" refers to oral nutritional supplements that are specifically designed to provide additional energy and protein to patients with particular dietary needs. These products are prescribed for individuals who are unable to achieve their nutritional goals through a traditional diet, including those who may have swallowing difficulties or are experiencing significant weight loss. 

Oral supplements are particularly relevant in the context of nutrition for frail elderly individuals and are indicated for patients with conditions such as diabetes, where regular food intake may not suffice to meet their energy and nutrient requirements. They are characterized by their high caloric content and are intended for patients with normal gastrointestinal function, ensuring that they can effectively enhance dietary intake. Overall, oral supplements serve as a vital tool in addressing nutritional deficiencies and supporting the health of patients with specific dietary challenges.CUIDADO E HIGIENE DE LA CAVIDAD ORAL:Oral care and hygiene practices are essential for patients with dysphagia to prevent complications such as aspiration pneumonia.PROGRAMAS FORMATIVOS:Training programs for patients and families that educate on managing dysphagia and ensuring safe eating practices.EVALUACI√ìN COMPLETA DEL ESTADO NUTRICIONAL:A comprehensive evaluation of a patient's nutritional status, including various assessments and tests to guide treatment.CIRUG√çA REPARADORA:Reparative surgery is performed to correct anatomical issues that may contribute to dysphagia.NUTRITIONAL RISK SCREENING:Nutritional Risk Screening refers to a systematic approach aimed at assessing the risk of malnutrition, particularly among older adults and patients in various healthcare settings. The Nutritional Risk Screening (NRS 2002) is a specific tool designed for this purpose, which helps identify individuals at risk of malnutrition, guiding healthcare professionals in implementing appropriate interventions to improve patient outcomes. This tool is especially relevant in hospitalized environments and is recommended for use in patients entering the Intensive Care Unit (ICU). A systematic review of nutritional screening tools highlights the importance of these assessments in predicting mortality and functional decline in older adults, underscoring the critical role of Nutritional Risk Screening in enhancing patient care and management.M√âTODO DE VOLUMEN-VISCOSIDAD:Volume-viscosity method is a technique used to assess swallowing function and determine safe food consistencies for patients.DIETA INICIAL DE DISFAGIA:Initial dysphagia diet consists of pureed foods designed for patients with swallowing difficulties.CUESTIONARIO SEMISTRUCTURADO:Semi-structured questionnaires are used to gather detailed dietary information from patients for nutritional assessment.CUIDADOS AMBIENTALES:Environmental care involves creating a safe eating environment for patients with dysphagia to minimize risks during meals.CUIDADOS POSTURALES:Postural care refers to the positioning of patients during eating to facilitate safe swallowing.GESTI√ìN DE LA COLOCACI√ìN DE SONDA:Management of feeding tube placement is crucial for patients requiring enteral nutrition.GESTI√ìN DE ACCESO VASCULAR:Management of vascular access is necessary for patients receiving total parenteral nutrition.)<|COMPLETE|>GASTROSTOM√çA:Gastrostom√≠a is a surgical procedure that involves creating an opening in the stomach to facilitate nutritional support through a feeding tube. This procedure is often employed when oral intake is not possible, particularly in patients with severe swallowing difficulties, esophageal obstruction, or other conditions that necessitate long-term nutritional support. It is commonly used in various clinical scenarios, including for patients with chronic conditions, those requiring prolonged feeding, and even in premature newborns.

The gastrostomy procedure typically involves placing a tube through the abdominal wall directly into the stomach, allowing for enteral feeding. This method ensures that patients receive adequate nutrition when they cannot eat by mouth, making it a critical intervention in managing nutritional needs. The procedure may be part of a broader treatment plan for individuals with severe dysphagia or low weight, as it provides a reliable means of nutritional intake.

In summary, gastrostom√≠a is a vital surgical intervention designed to support patients who require enteral nutrition, ensuring they receive the necessary sustenance for their health and well-being.EVALUACI√ìN FUNCIONAL:Functional evaluation is a process used to assess the capabilities of patients with dysphagia, involving various clinical techniques.TRATAMIENTO ESPEC√çFICO:Specific treatment refers to the tailored therapeutic approaches developed for patients with dysphagia based on their individual assessments.HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DE PONTEVEDRA (HUPA):HUPA is a hospital that collaborates with the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar√≠ngea to ensure the nutritional needs of patients are met through individualized dietary plans.EQUIPO DE NUTRICI√ìN CL√çNICA Y DIET√âTICA (UNCYD):The UNCyD team is responsible for assessing and monitoring the nutritional status of patients, ensuring appropriate dietary interventions are implemented.TEST DE VOLUMEN-VISCOSIDAD:The volume-viscosity test is a clinical evaluation performed by nursing staff to assess the swallowing capabilities of patients.ENDOCINOLOG√çA:The Endocrinolog√≠a (Endocrinology) service deals with hormonal and metabolic disorders, which can impact nutritional status and swallowing.CONSULTA PRIMERA DISFAGIA OROFAR√çNGEA:The Consulta Primera Disfagia Orofar√≠ngea is a specialized consultation for the initial assessment of patients suspected of having oropharyngeal dysphagia.VIDEOFLOUROSCOPIAS:Videofluoroscopias are diagnostic procedures performed to assess swallowing function in patients with dysphagia.MUST:The Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool (MUST) is a comprehensive screening tool designed to identify adults at risk of malnutrition. It is recommended by the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN) for use in community settings and various healthcare environments. MUST serves as a valuable resource for assessing nutritional risk in the general population, helping healthcare professionals to identify individuals who may be malnourished or at risk of malnutrition. This tool is particularly effective in screening patients and community members, facilitating early intervention and management of malnutrition. Overall, MUST is recognized as an essential instrument for evaluating nutritional status and addressing malnutrition risk among adults.MNA S-F:The Mini Nutritional Assessment Short-Form (MNA S-F) is a tool used to evaluate the nutritional status of elderly patients.ALIMENTOS SEGUROS:The safe foods provided by the Servicio de Cocina Hospitalaria for the evaluation of dysphagia include yogurt and custard.ALIMENTOS PELIGROSOS:"ALIMENTOS PELIGROSOS" refers to foods that pose significant risks for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. These dangerous foods include sticky items and those that can easily fragment, which may lead to choking or aspiration. Specifically, the foods identified as hazardous for individuals undergoing dysphagia assessment encompass orange, noodle soup, croquettes, meatballs in sauce, toasted bread, and cookies. It is crucial for caregivers and healthcare providers to be aware of these foods to ensure the safety and well-being of patients with swallowing difficulties.UNIDAD DE LOGOPEDIA:The Unidad de Logopedia (Speech Therapy Unit) provides rehabilitative treatment for patients with dysphagia.FISIOTERAPIA:The Fisioterapia (Physiotherapy) service may be involved in the rehabilitation of patients with dysphagia.ALZHEIMER:Alzheimer's disease is a progressive neurodegenerative disorder that primarily affects memory and cognitive function, leading to significant cognitive decline. It is characterized by the presence of beta-amyloid plaques in the brain and the degeneration of brain cells. This condition not only impacts the patient's ability to perform daily activities but also contributes to complications such as dysphagia and malnutrition. Various risk factors are associated with Alzheimer's disease, including cardiovascular disease, diabetes mellitus, and elevated levels of homocysteine. Additionally, dietary habits may influence the progression of the disease. Overall, Alzheimer's disease represents a serious neurological condition that poses challenges for both patients and caregivers.CUESTIONARIOS DE SATISFACCI√ìN:Satisfaction questionnaires are tools used to evaluate patient satisfaction with care and services received, helping to identify areas for improvement in healthcare delivery.GRD:KATIA SEVILLA:Katia Sevilla is a professional involved in interdisciplinary interventions related to dysphagia management.EIICHI SAITOH:Eiichi Saitoh is a researcher who contributed to the development of trans-disciplinary approaches for dysphagia rehabilitation in Japan.KOICHIRO MATSUNO:Koichiro Matsuno is a researcher involved in dysphagia rehabilitation studies in Japan.YOKO INAMOTO:Yoko Inamoto is a researcher who has worked on dysphagia rehabilitation in Japan.MAKOTO ISHIKAWA:Makoto Ishikawa is a researcher contributing to dysphagia rehabilitation approaches in Japan.AKIO TSUBAHARA:Akio Tsubahara is a researcher involved in the development of dysphagia rehabilitation methods in Japan.QASC TRIALISTS GROUP:The QASC Trialists Group is involved in implementing evidence-based treatment protocols for managing swallowing dysfunction in acute stroke patients.GESTI√ìN DEL CENTRO:Gesti√≥n del centro refers to the management practices within healthcare facilities that impact patient care and quality indicators.INDICADORES DE CALIDAD:"INDICADORES DE CALIDAD" refers to metrics utilized to evaluate the quality of care delivered in healthcare environments. These indicators are particularly significant in the context of dysphagia management, as they help ensure that patients receive appropriate and effective care. Overall, "indicadores de calidad" serve as essential tools for assessing the quality of healthcare services and patient care across various medical settings.DIETAS DE F√ÅCIL DEGLUC