¬;^R≠;C={e˚ª◊.º"…C=Eeº{"title": "PARKINSON'S DISEASE:Parkinson's disease is a neurodegenerative disorder that can lead to dysphagia, increasing the risk of aspiration and pneumonia."}{"title": "CANCER OF HEAD AND NECK:Cancer of the head and neck can affect swallowing and may require specific rehabilitation protocols to improve dysphagia."}{"title": "ELECTROSTIMULATION:Electrostimulation is a therapeutic technique used to enhance muscle function and prevent atrophy in patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "DEGLUTORY DISORDERS:Deglutory disorders refer to difficulties in swallowing, which can be treated through various rehabilitation techniques."}{"title": "EXERCISES FOR VOCAL CORDS:Exercises for vocal cords are included in rehabilitation protocols to improve glottic closure and reduce aspiration risk in patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "SHERKER EXERCISES:Shaker exercises are a specific type of exercise aimed at improving swallowing function in patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "CLINICAL TRIALS:Clinical trials are research studies that test the effectiveness of treatments, such as those for dysphagia in patients with head and neck cancer."}{"title": "SUPRA- AND INFRAHYOID MUSCLES:The supra- and infrahyoid muscles are groups of muscles in the neck that play a crucial role in swallowing and are targeted in dysphagia treatments."}{"title": "EXERCISES:Exercises are physical activities included in rehabilitation protocols to improve swallowing function in patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "NEUROMUSCULAR ELECTRICAL STIMULATION:Neuromuscular electrical stimulation is a technique used to enhance muscle activation in patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "CHATTANOOGA GROUP:Chattanooga Group is the company that developed the VitalStim\u00ae device for treating dysphagia through neuromuscular electrical stimulation."}{"title": "EQUIPO PROFESIONAL:The professional team includes doctors, nurses, and speech therapists who monitor and provide guidance for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "HIGIENE ORAL:Oral hygiene practices are essential for preventing respiratory infections in patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "EPILEPSIA:Epilepsia is a prominent medical journal dedicated to publishing research related to epilepsy and seizure disorders. It focuses on various aspects of epilepsy, including treatment approaches and dietary interventions, notably the ketogenic diet, which has been historically significant in managing the condition. The journal serves as a peer-reviewed platform for studies that explore the neurological manifestations of epilepsy, including its occurrence in specific patient populations, such as those with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes), where epilepsy contributes to their overall health challenges.\n\nEpilepsy itself is a neurological disorder characterized by recurrent seizures, which can significantly impact treatment strategies for affected individuals, including those with conditions like oropharyngeal dysphagia. The condition is recognized in both English and Spanish literature, emphasizing its global relevance and the importance of dietary management, such as the ketogenic diet, among other treatment methods. Overall, Epilepsia plays a crucial role in advancing the understanding and treatment of epilepsy through rigorous research and scholarly discourse."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N ASISTIDA:Assisted feeding techniques are important for patients with dysphagia to ensure safe and effective nutrition."}{"title": "DIFICULTADES COGNITIVAS:Cognitive difficulties can impact a patient's ability to follow swallowing instructions and manage dysphagia."}{"title": "TUMOR ACTIVO:"}{"title": "LANGMORE SE:Langmore SE is an author who contributed to the literature on the efficacy of exercises to rehabilitate dysphagia."}{"title": "PISENGA JM:Pisegna JM is an author who co-wrote a critique of the literature on dysphagia rehabilitation."}{"title": "HEGLAND KW:Hegland KW is an author who discussed nonsurgical treatment for swallowing rehabilitation."}{"title": "MURRY T:Murry T is an author who contributed to the discussion on nonsurgical treatment for swallowing rehabilitation."}{"title": "ROGUS-PULIA N:Rogus-Pulia N is a researcher who specializes in swallowing studies and has made significant contributions to the field of dysphagia rehabilitation. As an author, Rogus-Pulia N has focused on developing and promoting rehabilitation approaches specifically tailored for post-stroke patients experiencing difficulties with swallowing."}{"title": "ROBBINS J:Robbins J is an author who co-wrote on rehabilitation approaches for dysphagia."}{"title": "SUTTRUP I:Suttrup I is an author who studied dysphagia in Parkinson's Disease."}{"title": "NEWMAN R:Newman R is an author who wrote about the effect of bolus viscosity on swallowing safety and efficacy."}{"title": "VILARDELL N:Vilardell N is an author who co-wrote on bolus viscosity and swallowing."}{"title": "SPEYER R:Speyer R is an author who co-wrote on the effect of bolus viscosity on swallowing."}{"title": "LOGEMANN JA:Logemann JA is a prominent researcher and author recognized for her significant contributions to the field of swallowing disorders and interventions. She has extensively studied the treatment of oral and pharyngeal dysphagia, providing valuable insights and advancements in the management of these conditions. Her work has had a substantial impact on both clinical practices and academic research related to swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "ANDERSEN UT:Andersen UT is an author who reviewed texture modified foods for dysphagia."}{"title": "KJAERSGAARD A:Kjaersgaard A is an author who contributed to the review of texture modified foods."}{"title": "HANSEN T:Hansen T is an author who contributed to the review of texture modified foods."}{"title": "POULSEN I:Poulsen I is an author who contributed to the review of texture modified foods."}{"title": "YOUNG JL:Young JL is an author who studied the sequence of swallowing events."}{"title": "MACRAE P:Macrae P is an author who co-wrote on the sequence of swallowing events."}{"title": "ANDERSON C:Anderson C is an author who co-wrote on the sequence of swallowing events."}{"title": "TAYLOR-KAMARA I:Taylor-Kamara I is an author who co-wrote on the sequence of swallowing events."}{"title": "HUMBERT IA:Humbert IA is an author who co-wrote on the sequence of swallowing events."}{"title": "SHANAHAN TK:Shanahan TK is an author who studied the effect of chin-down posture on aspiration in dysphagic patients."}{"title": "PAULOSKI BR:Pauloski BR is a researcher and author known for their contributions to the field of swallowing disorders, particularly in cancer patients. They studied the effects of enhanced bolus flavors on oropharyngeal swallow, aiming to improve the swallowing experience for individuals undergoing treatment. Additionally, Pauloski BR co-wrote a publication that examined the effects of chin-down posture on aspiration, further highlighting their expertise in the dynamics of swallowing and aspiration risk management."}{"title": "RADEMAKER AW:Rademaker AW is a researcher and author known for significant contributions to the field of swallowing, particularly in patients who have undergone treatment for head and neck cancer. Rademaker AW has co-authored studies that explore the effects of chin-down posture on aspiration, furthering the understanding of swallowing mechanics and rehabilitation in this patient population."}{"title": "KAHRILAS PJ:Kahrilas PJ is an author who co-wrote on chin-down posture effects on aspiration."}{"title": "LEIGH JH:Leigh JH is an author who studied the influence of chin-down and chin-tuck maneuvers on swallowing kinematics."}{"title": "OH BM:Oh BM is an author who co-wrote on the influence of chin-down and chin-tuck maneuvers."}{"title": "SEO HG:Seo HG is an author who co-wrote on the influence of chin-down and chin-tuck maneuvers."}{"title": "LEE GJ:Lee GJ is an author who co-wrote on the influence of chin-down and chin-tuck maneuvers."}{"title": "MIN Y:Min Y is an author who co-wrote on the influence of chin-down and chin-tuck maneuvers."}{"title": "KIM K:Kim K is an author who co-wrote on the influence of chin-down and chin-tuck maneuvers."}{"title": "MANUAL DE DISFAGIA OROFAR(\"ENTITY\":"}{"title": "ANN REHABIL MED:Ann Rehabil Med is a medical journal that publishes research related to rehabilitation medicine, including studies on swallowing disorders."}{"title": "HEAD NECK:Head & Neck is a medical journal dedicated to the study and research of head and neck cancers and their treatment. It emphasizes the impact of these conditions on various aspects of patient health, particularly focusing on swallowing issues that arise in cancer patients. The journal covers a wide range of topics related to head and neck surgery and oncology, providing valuable insights into the challenges and advancements in the field."}{"title": "CODAS:Codas is a journal that publishes articles on communication disorders, including studies on swallowing and dysphagia."}{"title": "ARQ GASTROENTEROL:Arq Gastroenterol is a journal that publishes research related to gastroenterology, including studies on swallowing and dysphagia."}{"title": "CURRENT OPINION OTOLARYNGOL HEAD NECK SURG:Current Opinion in Otolaryngology and Head and Neck Surgery is a journal that discusses current trends and research in otolaryngology, including swallowing disorders."}{"title": "FOLIA PHONIATR LOGOP:Folia Phoniatrica et Logopaedica is a journal that publishes research on speech and language pathology, including studies on swallowing."}{"title": "J SPEECH LANG HEAR RES:Journal of Speech, Language, and Hearing Research is a journal that publishes research on communication disorders, including swallowing issues."}{"title": "AM J SPEECH LANG PATHOL:American Journal of Speech-Language Pathology is a journal that publishes research on speech and language disorders, including dysphagia."}{"title": "ARCH PHYS MED REHABIL:Archives of Physical Medicine and Rehabilitation is a journal that publishes research on rehabilitation, including studies on swallowing therapies."}{"title": "IOWA ORAL PERFORMANCE INSTRUMENT:The Iowa Oral Performance Instrument (IOPI) is a specialized device designed for diagnosing and training the strength and endurance of the tongue and lips, particularly in patients with swallowing disorders. It is utilized to measure both tongue and hand strength and endurance, making it relevant in various studies related to dysphagia. The IOPI serves as a valuable tool in dysphagia research, aiding in the assessment and treatment of individuals experiencing difficulties with swallowing."}{"title": "RYU JS:Ryu JS is a researcher involved in the study of pharyngeal pressure events using high-resolution manometry."}{"title": "SONG SH:Song SH is a researcher who co-authored the study on head rotation and head tilt effects on swallowing."}{"title": "KOO JH:Koo JH is a researcher who contributed to the study on pharyngeal pressure events."}{"title": "LEE KD:Lee KD is a researcher involved in the study of swallowing mechanics."}{"title": "PARK HS:Park HS is a researcher who co-authored the study on the effects of head rotation and tilt on swallowing."}{"title": "LUNDY D:Lundy D is a researcher involved in the study of swallowing in head and neck cancer patients."}{"title": "SULLIVAN PA:Sullivan PA is a researcher who studied the effects of bolus flavors on swallowing."}{"title": "NEWMAN LA:Newman LA is a researcher who contributed to the study on oropharyngeal swallow in cancer patients."}{"title": "GATTO AR:Gatto AR is a researcher who studied the effects of sour taste and cold temperature on swallowing in stroke patients."}{"title": "COLA PC:Cola PC is a researcher involved in studies on swallowing and its mechanics."}{"title": "SILVA RG:Silva RG is a researcher who co-authored studies on swallowing in stroke patients."}{"title": "SPADOTTO AA:Spadotto AA is a researcher who studied the effects of temperature and taste on swallowing."}{"title": "RIBEIRO PW:Ribeiro PW is a researcher involved in swallowing studies related to stroke."}{"title": "SCHELP AO:Schelp AO is a researcher who contributed to studies on swallowing mechanics."}{"title": "HENRY MA:Henry MA is a researcher involved in studies on swallowing and its physiological aspects."}{"title": "REGAN J:Regan J is a researcher who studied the effects of thermal-tactile stimulation on swallowing in Parkinson's disease."}{"title": "WALSHE M:Walshe M is a researcher involved in swallowing studies related to Parkinson's disease."}{"title": "TOBIN WO:Tobin WO is a researcher who studied the timing of swallow in idiopathic Parkinson's disease."}{"title": "ROFES L:Rofes L is a researcher who studied the effects of natural capsaicinoids on swallowing response in older patients."}{"title": "MARTIN A:Martin A is a researcher who contributed to studies on swallowing in older patients."}{"title": "CRARY MA:Crary MA is a researcher known for their work in the field of swallowing disorders, particularly focusing on the adoption of therapies to manage these conditions. Additionally, Crary MA is recognized as one of the authors of the Functional Oral Intake Scale, which is specifically designed for assessing dysphagia in stroke patients. This scale plays a crucial role in evaluating and guiding the treatment of individuals with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "CARNABY GD:Carnaby GD is a researcher involved in swallowing rehabilitation studies."}{"title": "LAZARUS C:Lazarus C is a researcher who studied the effects of maneuvers on swallowing function."}{"title": "CHAUDHURI G:Chaudhuri G is a researcher who studied cardiovascular effects of swallowing maneuvers in stroke patients."}{"title": "HILDNER CD:Hildner CD is a researcher involved in swallowing studies related to stroke."}{"title": "BRADY S:Brady S is a researcher who studied swallowing maneuvers in stroke patients."}{"title": "HUTCHINS B:Hutchins B is a researcher involved in swallowing studies."}{"title": "ALIGA N:Aliga N is a researcher who contributed to studies on swallowing maneuvers."}{"title": "ABADILLA E:Abadilla E is a researcher involved in swallowing studies."}{"title": "WHEELER-HEGLAND KM:Wheeler-Hegland KM is a researcher who studied submental sEMG and hyoid movement during swallowing maneuvers."}{"title": "ROSENBEK JC:Rosenbek JC is a researcher involved in swallowing studies."}{"title": "SAPIENZA CM:Sapienza CM is a researcher who studied swallowing maneuvers and their effects."}{"title": "FUKUOKA T:Fukuoka T is a researcher who studied the effects of effortful swallow and Mendelsohn maneuver on tongue pressure."}{"title": "ONO T:Ono T is a researcher involved in swallowing studies."}{"title": "HORI K:Hori K is a researcher who studied swallowing biomechanics."}{"title": "TAMINE K:Tamine K is a researcher involved in swallowing studies."}{"title": "NOZAKI S:Nozaki S is a researcher who studied swallowing mechanics."}{"title": "SHIMADA K:Shimada K is a researcher involved in swallowing studies."}{"title": "YAMAMOTO N:Yamamoto N is a researcher who studied swallowing mechanics."}{"title": "FUKUDA Y:Fukuda Y is a researcher involved in swallowing studies."}{"title": "DOMEN K:Domen K is a researcher who studied swallowing mechanics."}{"title": "LENIUS K:Lenius K is a researcher who studied the effects of lingual effort on swallow pressures."}{"title": "STIERWALT J:Stierwalt J is a researcher involved in swallowing studies."}{"title": "LAPOINTE LL:LaPointe LL is a researcher who studied swallowing mechanics."}{"title": "BOURGEOIS M:Bourgeois M is a researcher involved in swallowing studies."}{"title": "CARNABY G:Carnaby G is a researcher who studied swallowing rehabilitation."}{"title": "CRARY M:Crary M is a researcher involved in swallowing studies."}{"title": "ADAMS V:Adams V is a researcher who conducted a systematic review on tongue and hand strength in swallowing."}{"title": "MATHISEN B:Mathisen B is a researcher involved in swallowing studies."}{"title": "BAINES S:Baines S is a researcher who studied swallowing mechanics."}{"title": "CALLISTER R:Callister R is a researcher involved in swallowing studies."}{"title": "RUSCHE N:Rusche N is a researcher who studied swallowing mechanics."}{"title": "HIND JA:Hind JA is a researcher involved in swallowing studies."}{"title": "J AM GERIATR SOC:The Journal of the American Geriatrics Society (J AM GERIATR SOC) is a prominent publication that focuses on research related to aging and health issues affecting older adults. It publishes a variety of studies, including those examining the relationship between testosterone levels and frailty in older men, as well as research on dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. Through its diverse range of articles, the journal aims to advance the understanding of geriatric health and improve the quality of care for the aging population."}{"title": "J PHYS THER SCI:The Journal of Physical Therapy Science publishes research on physical therapy practices, including studies on swallowing therapies."}{"title": "OTOLARYNGOL HEAD NECK SURG:Otolaryngology - Head and Neck Surgery is a journal that publishes research on conditions affecting the ear, nose, throat, and related structures, including dysphagia."}{"title": "AM J PHYS MED REHABIL:The American Journal of Physical Medicine & Rehabilitation publishes research on rehabilitation practices, including studies on dysphagia in stroke patients."}{"title": "CLIN REHABIL:Clinical Rehabilitation is a journal that publishes research on rehabilitation practices, including studies on dysphagia and related therapies."}{"title": "RESEARCH GROUP FOR ASPIRATION PNEUMONIA:The Research Group for Aspiration Pneumonia is a collective focused on studying aspiration pneumonia, particularly in the elderly and its relation to dysphagia."}{"title": "PETERS K:Peters K is a researcher involved in studies on dysphagia and rehabilitation techniques."}{"title": "EROGLU ST:Eroglu ST is a researcher who has worked on neuromuscular electrical stimulation for dysphagia in stroke patients."}{"title": "PERLESS-CARROLL M:Perless-Carroll M is a researcher contributing to studies on dysphagia rehabilitation."}{"title": "JOHNSON-GREENE D:Johnson-Greene D is a researcher involved in the study of dysphagia and rehabilitation methods."}{"title": "CHEN YW:Chen YW is a researcher who has conducted studies on the effects of neuromuscular electrical stimulation on post-stroke dysphagia."}{"title": "CHANG KH:Chang KH is a researcher involved in studies related to dysphagia and rehabilitation."}{"title": "CHEN HC:Chen HC is a researcher who has contributed to studies on dysphagia and its treatments."}{"title": "LIANG WM:Liang WM is a researcher involved in studies on dysphagia and rehabilitation techniques."}{"title": "WANG YH:Wang YH is a researcher who has worked on studies related to dysphagia."}{"title": "LIN YN:Lin YN is a researcher contributing to studies on dysphagia and rehabilitation."}{"title": "TAN C:Tan C is a researcher who has conducted meta-analyses on dysphagia treatments."}{"title": "LIU Y:Liu Y is a researcher involved in studies on dysphagia and its rehabilitation."}{"title": "LIU J:Liu J is a prominent researcher and author who has made significant contributions to the field of medical research. Liu J co-authored a study published in the International Journal of Surgery, which examined the effect of early oral feeding on the short-term outcomes of patients undergoing laparoscopic distal gastrectomy. In addition to this work, Liu J has focused on dysphagia treatments, contributing valuable insights into this area of study. Furthermore, Liu J conducted a meta-analysis investigating the relationship between fruit and vegetable intake and esophageal squamous cell carcinoma, as well as studying the impact of fruit and vegetable consumption on lung cancer. Through these diverse research efforts, Liu J has demonstrated a commitment to advancing knowledge in oncology and surgical outcomes."}{"title": "CHEN L:Chen L is a researcher involved in studies on dysphagia and rehabilitation techniques."}{"title": "BHATT AD:Bhatt AD is a researcher who has studied the impact of electrical stimulation on dysphagia in patients with head and neck cancer."}{"title": "GOODWIN N:Goodwin N is a researcher contributing to studies on dysphagia and its treatments."}{"title": "CASH E:Cash E is a researcher involved in studies related to dysphagia."}{"title": "BHATT G:Bhatt G is a researcher who has worked on studies related to dysphagia treatments."}{"title": "SILVERMAN CL:Silverman CL is a researcher contributing to studies on dysphagia and rehabilitation."}{"title": "SPANOS WJ:Spanos WJ is a researcher involved in studies on dysphagia and its treatments.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "UFDOF:The Functional Unit of Oropharyngeal Dysphagia (UFDOF), also known as Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar\u00edngea, is a specialized unit located within HUPA (Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias) in the Community of Madrid. This unit is dedicated to the evaluation, diagnosis, and treatment of patients suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. In addition to providing direct patient care, UFDOF is committed to training healthcare professionals to enhance the quality of care for individuals with dysphagia. Through its focused approach, UFDOF aims to improve the management of swallowing disorders and ensure comprehensive support for affected patients."}{"title": "JAPANESE SOCIETY OF DYSPHAGIA REHABILITATION:The Japanese Society of Dysphagia Rehabilitation (JSDR) is an organization that advocates for a transdisciplinary approach in the rehabilitation of dysphagia."}{"title": "LOGOPEDIA:Logopedia refers to the field of speech therapy that encompasses services aimed at the treatment of dysphagia, a condition that affects an individual's ability to swallow. It plays a crucial role in the rehabilitation of patients suffering from this disorder, providing essential support and therapeutic interventions to improve their swallowing capabilities and overall communication skills."}{"title": "TERAPIA OCUPACIONAL:Terapia Ocupacional (Occupational Therapy) is a discipline that plays a significant role in the rehabilitation of patients with dysphagia. The Terapia Ocupacional service specifically focuses on assisting these patients in their recovery process, utilizing various therapeutic techniques to improve their swallowing abilities and overall quality of life."}{"title": "ENFERMER\u00cdA:Enfermer\u00eda (Nursing) provides essential support in the care of patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects the ability to swallow. The nursing staff plays a crucial role in assessing patients and implementing dietary modifications as part of the treatment for swallowing disorders. Specifically, the nursing team is instrumental in the assessment and care of patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia within the hospital setting. Their expertise and interventions are vital for ensuring the well-being and recovery of these patients."}{"title": "NEUR\u00d3LOGOS:Neur\u00f3logos (Neurologists) are specialists involved in the assessment and treatment of dysphagia-related conditions."}{"title": "DIETISTAS AMERICANAS:Dietistas Americanas, or American Dietitians, are professionals who offer dietary advice and support specifically for patients experiencing dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing."}{"title": "EQUIPO INTERDISCIPLINAR:An interdisciplinary team is a group of professionals from various disciplines working together to address a specific patient situation in dysphagia treatment."}{"title": "EQUIPO MULTIDISCIPLINAR:The \"EQUIPO MULTIDISCIPLINAR\" is a multidisciplinary team composed of various healthcare professionals, including a psychiatrist, psychologist, endocrinologist, diabetes educator, dietitian/nutritionist, and social worker. This team collaborates to manage treatment priorities for patients with diabetes and eating disorders, ensuring comprehensive care tailored to individual needs. Additionally, the team includes professionals from different specialties who work together to provide care for patients with dysphagia and those requiring home parenteral nutrition. Furthermore, the team is involved in designing appropriate diets for patients in the context of renal insufficiency, highlighting their commitment to addressing diverse health challenges through a collaborative approach."}{"title": "EQUIPO TRANSDISCIPLINAR:A transdisciplinary team goes beyond traditional roles, allowing professionals to take on tasks from other disciplines to enhance patient care in dysphagia."}{"title": "ATENCI\u00d3N INTEGRAL:Atenci\u00f3n integral refers to the comprehensive care approach provided to patients with dysphagia, involving multiple disciplines."}{"title": "PROFESIONALES DE LA SALUD:\"PROFESIONALES DE LA SALUD\" refers to healthcare professionals who play a crucial role in providing medical services and support to patients. They are essential for the diagnosis and treatment of various conditions, including oropharyngeal dysphagia. These professionals are specifically involved in the treatment and rehabilitation of patients suffering from dysphagia, ensuring that individuals receive the necessary care and support to manage their condition effectively."}{"title": "ABORDAJE DE LA DISFAGIA:Abordaje de la disfagia refers to the strategies and methods used to treat and manage dysphagia."}{"title": "INTERVENCI\u00d3N CONJUNTA:Intervenci\u00f3n conjunta refers to the collaborative approach taken by various professionals in treating dysphagia."}{"title": "EVALUACI\u00d3N DE PATOLOG\u00cdAS:Evaluaci\u00f3n de patolog\u00edas refers to the assessment of medical conditions, including dysphagia, by a team of specialists."}{"title": "ENFOQUE MULTIDISCIPLINARIO:Enfoque multidisciplinario refers to the collaborative method involving multiple disciplines to address dysphagia treatment."}{"title": "VISI\u00d3N COMPLETA:Visi\u00f3n completa refers to the comprehensive perspective gained through a multidisciplinary approach in dysphagia care.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "NEUROLOG\u00cdA:The entity \"NEUROLOG\u00cdA\" refers to a specialized unit within a hospital dedicated to the diagnosis and treatment of disorders related to the nervous system. This department plays a crucial role in addressing various neurological conditions, including those that may lead to complications such as dysphagia, which is difficulty in swallowing. Through its comprehensive approach, the Neurology department aims to manage and treat the underlying causes of these disorders effectively."}{"title": "MEDICINA INTERNA:The \"MEDICINA INTERNA\" refers to the Internal Medicine department, which is a medical specialty focused on the diagnosis, treatment, and prevention of diseases in adults. This specialty encompasses a wide range of conditions affecting multiple systems of the body. The department is particularly noted for its role in managing patients with dysphagia, ensuring coordinated care for these individuals. Additionally, the Internal Medicine department emphasizes dietary considerations as part of its comprehensive care approach for adult patients. Overall, \"MEDICINA INTERNA\" plays a crucial role in providing thorough medical attention and support for various adult health issues."}{"title": "ONCOLOG\u00cdA:The Oncology department addresses dysphagia in patients with cancer-related complications."}{"title": "ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:\"ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N\" is a specialized field of medicine that focuses on hormonal and nutritional health. It encompasses both clinical practice and research, as evidenced by the existence of a scientific journal dedicated to this discipline. The journal, also named \"Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n,\" serves as a platform for disseminating research findings related to endocrinology and nutrition. \n\nIn clinical settings, the Endocrinology and Nutrition department plays a crucial role in patient care, particularly for individuals with diabetes and those requiring nutritional support, such as dysphagia patients. This department is where patients are referred for evaluation after experiencing significant weight loss, highlighting its importance in managing various health concerns related to nutrition and hormonal balance.\n\nMart\u00edn L\u00f3pez de la Torre Casares is noted for his specialization in this field, contributing to both the clinical and editorial aspects of endocrinology and nutrition. As an associate editor of the journal, he is involved in advancing knowledge and research in this vital area of healthcare."}{"title": "LOGOPEDAS:Logopedas are professionals who specialize in the evaluation and treatment of swallowing disorders, particularly in patients with dysphagia. They play a crucial role in assessing deglutition and the risk of aspiration in individuals receiving enteral nutrition. In both the United States and Europe, logopedas are primarily responsible for the care of patients with dysphagia, ensuring that these individuals receive appropriate interventions to manage their swallowing difficulties effectively."}{"title": "UNCYD:The Unidad de Nutrici\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica y Diet\u00e9tica (UNCyD) is a clinical nutrition unit dedicated to conducting nutritional assessments and screenings, particularly for patients over the age of 65. It operates within a team-oriented framework, offering nutritional support tailored to individuals with special needs. UNCyD focuses on the management of clinical nutrition and dietary practices to enhance patient care and well-being."}{"title": "COMUNIDAD DE MADRID:The Community of Madrid is an autonomous community in Spain that serves as a significant healthcare hub. It is home to the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias (HUPA), which acts as a reference center for the treatment of patients suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia. Additionally, the region is notable for its specific measurement and reporting of congenital hypothyroidism incidence, highlighting its commitment to monitoring and addressing health issues within the population. Overall, the Community of Madrid plays a crucial role in providing specialized medical services and healthcare resources to its residents."}{"title": "EQUIPO DE DIRECCI\u00d3N:The Equipo de Direcci\u00f3n is the management team at the Hospital Universitario Pr\u00edncipe de Asturias responsible for overseeing the implementation of new healthcare initiatives."}{"title": "PROFESIONALES SANITARIOS:Healthcare professionals involved in the management of patients with DOF, including nurses, dietitians, speech therapists, and medical specialists."}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICOS EN ALIMENTACI\u00d3N Y DIET\u00c9TICA:Dietitians and nutrition technicians who assist in the dietary management of patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "M\u00c9DICOS ESPECIALISTAS EN ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:Medical specialists in endocrinology and nutrition who provide care for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "ESPECIALISTAS EN OTORRINOLARINGOLOG\u00cdA:Otolaryngology specialists who are involved in diagnosing and treating swallowing disorders."}{"title": "ESPECIALISTAS EN REHABILITACI\u00d3N:Rehabilitation specialists who assist in the recovery and management of patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "FAR\u00cdNGEA:FAR\u00cdNGEA is an organization focused on multidisciplinary solutions in the Community of Madrid, dedicated to the professional development of its personnel."}{"title": "HUPA:HUPA is a healthcare center dedicated to the eradication of dysphagia and malnutrition, with a strong commitment to enhancing patient care through multidisciplinary approaches. Located in the Community of Madrid, HUPA oversees the Functional Unit of Orofar\u00edngea Dysphagia, offering specialized care for patients suffering from oropharyngeal dysphagia. The institution emphasizes comprehensive and quality treatment, ensuring that patients receive thorough evaluation and management of their swallowing disorders. In addition to its focus on dysphagia, HUPA provides a range of medical services aimed at improving overall patient health and well-being."}{"title": "ALCAL\u00c1 DE HENARES:Alcal\u00e1 de Henares is the head city of the Community of Madrid where the Functional Unit of Orofar\u00edngea Dysphagia is located."}{"title": "COMUNIDAD AUT\u00d3NOMA DE MADRID:The Community of Madrid is the autonomous community where the UFDOF operates, providing healthcare services to its population."}{"title": "CALIDAD ASISTENCIAL:Calidad asistencial refers to the quality of care provided to patients, encompassing various dimensions such as accessibility, equity, and effectiveness. It is particularly relevant in the context of managing specific conditions, such as dysphagia. Additionally, calidad asistencial represents the standard of care that the UFDOF aims to provide to its patients, ensuring that all aspects of patient care meet high-quality benchmarks."}{"title": "INNOVACI\u00d3N:Innovaci\u00f3n refers to the commitment of the UFDOF to incorporate innovative practices in the treatment of dysphagia."}{"title": "INVESTIGACI\u00d3N:Investigaci\u00f3n refers to the research efforts that the UFDOF is committed to in order to improve dysphagia treatment. Additionally, it encompasses the study of artificial home nutrition, which is necessary to determine its impact on quality of life and the early detection of mood disorders. This comprehensive approach highlights the importance of research in both enhancing treatment methods and understanding the broader implications of nutritional interventions on health and well-being."}{"title": "DOCENCIA:Docencia refers to the educational activities that the UFDOF engages in to train healthcare professionals."}{"title": "OTORRINOLARINGOLOGY:The Otorrinolaringolog\u00eda service at HUPA specializes in ear, nose, and throat conditions, contributing to the multidisciplinary approach to dysphagia."}{"title": "REHABILITATION:Rehabilitation refers to the process of restoring health and functional ability in patients with chronic diseases through various therapeutic interventions, including nutritional support. The Rehabilitation service at HUPA specifically focuses on the recovery and rehabilitation of patients, including those who experience dysphagia, ensuring a comprehensive approach to patient care and recovery."}{"title": "NUTRITION CLINICAL AND DIETETICS:The Nutrition Clinical and Dietetics service at HUPA provides dietary support and nutritional care for patients, particularly those with dysphagia."}{"title": "HOSPITAL KITCHEN SERVICE:The Hospital Kitchen Service at HUPA prepares meals tailored to the needs of patients, including those with dysphagia."}{"title": "LOGOPEDIST:A logopedist at HUPA specializes in speech and language therapy, playing a crucial role in the care of patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "NURSES:Nurses at HUPA are trained in Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics, providing essential care for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "COOKS:Cooks at HUPA prepare meals that meet the dietary needs of patients, including those with dysphagia."}{"title": "UNIT OF OROPHARYNGEAL DYSPHAGIA:The Unit of Oropharyngeal Dysphagia at HUPA is dedicated to providing multidisciplinary care for patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "SERVICIO DE ORL:The Servicio de ORL (Otorhinolaryngology Service) at HUPA is dedicated to the diagnosis and treatment of conditions affecting the ear, nose, and throat. This includes a focus on swallowing disorders, specifically dysphagia. The service provides specialized care and assessments for patients with these conditions and collaborates with the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar\u00edngea to enhance patient outcomes. Through its comprehensive approach, the Servicio de ORL ensures that patients receive targeted and effective treatment for their otorhinolaryngological needs."}{"title": "SERVICIO DE REHABILITACI\u00d3N:The Rehabilitation Service at HUPA provides therapeutic interventions for patients recovering from various conditions, including swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "SERVICIO DE COCINA HOSPITALARIA:The Servicio de Cocina Hospitalaria at HUPA is dedicated to preparing and providing meals that are specifically tailored to meet the dietary needs of patients. This includes accommodating individuals undergoing swallowing assessments and ensuring that all meals align with the individualized diets prescribed by the UNCyD team. The service focuses on delivering nutrition that supports the health and recovery of patients, taking into account their unique nutritional requirements."}{"title": "CATALU\u00d1A:Catalu\u00f1a is an autonomous community in Spain known for its comprehensive approach to public health and nutrition. In this region, administrative tools are available for hiring dietitians within the public health system, ensuring that nutritional needs are adequately addressed. Additionally, Catalu\u00f1a has been the site of significant research, including studies on iron deficiency and overload among the adult population, highlighting its commitment to understanding and improving health outcomes. For patients requiring ongoing nutritional treatment, it is necessary to submit a justification report to the relevant primary care center, which underscores the region's structured approach to healthcare management. Furthermore, the dispensing of nutritional and dietary products, referred to as NED products, is facilitated through hospital pharmacies, and there are established agreements with the pharmaceutical industry to enable home delivery, enhancing accessibility for patients in need."}{"title": "VIDEOFUOROSCOPIA DE LA DEGLUCI\u00d3N:Videofluoroscopy of swallowing is a diagnostic test performed to evaluate swallowing disorders, conducted in the UFDOF unit."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS S\u00d3LIDOS:Solid foods of various textures are prepared for patients undergoing swallowing assessments at HUPA."}{"title": "MATERIAL PARA REALIZAR LOS TEST DE VOLUMEN-VISCOSIDAD:Materials for conducting volume-viscosity tests are used in the assessment of swallowing disorders at HUPA."}{"title": "NAVARRA:Navarra is an autonomous community in Spain known for its distinct characteristics and health statistics. It is notable for having one of the lowest mortality rates for Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD) among women, indicating a relatively favorable health outcome in this demographic. Additionally, in Navarra, patients are required to submit a justification report to continue receiving treatment for their nutritional needs, reflecting the region's structured approach to healthcare management and patient support."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL TOTAL:NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL TOTAL, also known as Total Parenteral Nutrition (TPN), is a medical treatment that provides 100% of a patient's nutritional requirements through intravenous administration. This method is utilized when enteral nutrition is contraindicated or not tolerated, allowing nutrients to be delivered directly into the bloodstream, thereby bypassing the gastrointestinal tract. TPN is particularly important for patients who are unable to eat by mouth, ensuring they receive essential nutrients for their health and recovery.\n\nIn specific cases, such as when a patient loses their nasoenteric tube, TPN may be initiated to support their nutritional needs until they can resume oral feeding. This treatment serves as a critical intervention during hospitalization, ensuring that patients receive adequate nutritional support when traditional feeding methods are not viable. Overall, NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL TOTAL is a vital component of patient care for those requiring specialized nutritional support."}{"title": "EVALUACI\u00d3N NUTRICIONAL:EVALUACI\u00d3N NUTRICIONAL refers to the process of determining an individual's nutritional status through various measurements and analyses. This comprehensive evaluation is crucial for identifying dietary needs and nutritional support requirements, particularly for patients. It involves assessing a patient's dietary intake and overall nutritional status to ensure appropriate care is provided. This process is especially significant for individuals diagnosed with gastrointestinal cancers, as their nutritional needs may be more complex and require tailored interventions."}{"title": "ELECTROESTIMULACI\u00d3N:Electrostimulation is a therapeutic technique used in the rehabilitation of swallowing disorders."}{"title": "TOXINA BOTUL\u00cdNICA:Botulinum toxin, commonly known as \"TOXINA BOTUL\u00cdNICA,\" is utilized in specific medical applications to address various health issues. It is employed in the treatment of bowel function disorders, helping to manage conditions that affect gastrointestinal motility. Additionally, botulinum toxin is used in targeted therapies for oropharyngeal dysphagia, a condition that impairs swallowing function, thereby improving the ability to swallow in affected individuals."}{"title": "MIOTOM\u00cdA DEL CRICOFAR\u00cdNGEO:Cricopharyngeal myotomy is a surgical procedure aimed at improving swallowing by cutting the muscle at the top of the esophagus."}{"title": "HISTORIA CL\u00cdNICA:HISTORIA CL\u00cdNICA refers to the comprehensive medical history of a patient, which is essential for assessing and treating various health conditions, including dysphagia and diarrhea. It encompasses a detailed record of the patient's medical background, including dietary history and other relevant health information. The historia cl\u00ednica serves as a crucial document that not only tracks all follow-ups and treatments but also records the patient's health history and their responses to treatments. This medical record is fundamental for nutritional assessment and plays a vital role in guiding healthcare decisions related to the patient's treatment."}{"title": "VALORACI\u00d3N FUNCIONAL:Functional assessment involves evaluating a patient's physical capabilities, which is important in the context of dysphagia treatment."}{"title": "MEN\u00daS ALIMENTARIOS:Dietary menus are tailored food plans designed for patients with dysphagia, ensuring safe and appropriate food textures."}{"title": "SUPLEMENTOS ORALES:\"SUPLEMENTOS ORALES\" refers to oral nutritional supplements that are specifically designed to provide additional energy and protein to patients with particular dietary needs. These products are prescribed for individuals who are unable to achieve their nutritional goals through a traditional diet, including those who may have swallowing difficulties or are experiencing significant weight loss. \n\nOral supplements are particularly relevant in the context of nutrition for frail elderly individuals and are indicated for patients with conditions such as diabetes, where regular food intake may not suffice to meet their energy and nutrient requirements. They are characterized by their high caloric content and are intended for patients with normal gastrointestinal function, ensuring that they can effectively enhance dietary intake. Overall, oral supplements serve as a vital tool in addressing nutritional deficiencies and supporting the health of patients with specific dietary challenges."}{"title": "CUIDADO E HIGIENE DE LA CAVIDAD ORAL:Oral care and hygiene practices are essential for patients with dysphagia to prevent complications such as aspiration pneumonia."}{"title": "PROGRAMAS FORMATIVOS:Training programs for patients and families that educate on managing dysphagia and ensuring safe eating practices."}{"title": "EVALUACI\u00d3N COMPLETA DEL ESTADO NUTRICIONAL:A comprehensive evaluation of a patient's nutritional status, including various assessments and tests to guide treatment."}{"title": "CIRUG\u00cdA REPARADORA:Reparative surgery is performed to correct anatomical issues that may contribute to dysphagia."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL RISK SCREENING:Nutritional Risk Screening refers to a systematic approach aimed at assessing the risk of malnutrition, particularly among older adults and patients in various healthcare settings. The Nutritional Risk Screening (NRS 2002) is a specific tool designed for this purpose, which helps identify individuals at risk of malnutrition, guiding healthcare professionals in implementing appropriate interventions to improve patient outcomes. This tool is especially relevant in hospitalized environments and is recommended for use in patients entering the Intensive Care Unit (ICU). A systematic review of nutritional screening tools highlights the importance of these assessments in predicting mortality and functional decline in older adults, underscoring the critical role of Nutritional Risk Screening in enhancing patient care and management."}{"title": "M\u00c9TODO DE VOLUMEN-VISCOSIDAD:Volume-viscosity method is a technique used to assess swallowing function and determine safe food consistencies for patients."}{"title": "DIETA INICIAL DE DISFAGIA:Initial dysphagia diet consists of pureed foods designed for patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "CUESTIONARIO SEMISTRUCTURADO:Semi-structured questionnaires are used to gather detailed dietary information from patients for nutritional assessment."}{"title": "CUIDADOS AMBIENTALES:Environmental care involves creating a safe eating environment for patients with dysphagia to minimize risks during meals."}{"title": "CUIDADOS POSTURALES:Postural care refers to the positioning of patients during eating to facilitate safe swallowing."}{"title": "GESTI\u00d3N DE LA COLOCACI\u00d3N DE SONDA:Management of feeding tube placement is crucial for patients requiring enteral nutrition."}{"title": "GESTI\u00d3N DE ACCESO VASCULAR:Management of vascular access is necessary for patients receiving total parenteral nutrition.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "GASTROSTOM\u00cdA:Gastrostom\u00eda is a surgical procedure that involves creating an opening in the stomach to facilitate nutritional support through a feeding tube. This procedure is often employed when oral intake is not possible, particularly in patients with severe swallowing difficulties, esophageal obstruction, or other conditions that necessitate long-term nutritional support. It is commonly used in various clinical scenarios, including for patients with chronic conditions, those requiring prolonged feeding, and even in premature newborns.\n\nThe gastrostomy procedure typically involves placing a tube through the abdominal wall directly into the stomach, allowing for enteral feeding. This method ensures that patients receive adequate nutrition when they cannot eat by mouth, making it a critical intervention in managing nutritional needs. The procedure may be part of a broader treatment plan for individuals with severe dysphagia or low weight, as it provides a reliable means of nutritional intake.\n\nIn summary, gastrostom\u00eda is a vital surgical intervention designed to support patients who require enteral nutrition, ensuring they receive the necessary sustenance for their health and well-being."}{"title": "EVALUACI\u00d3N FUNCIONAL:Functional evaluation is a process used to assess the capabilities of patients with dysphagia, involving various clinical techniques."}{"title": "TRATAMIENTO ESPEC\u00cdFICO:Specific treatment refers to the tailored therapeutic approaches developed for patients with dysphagia based on their individual assessments."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO DE PONTEVEDRA (HUPA):HUPA is a hospital that collaborates with the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofar\u00edngea to ensure the nutritional needs of patients are met through individualized dietary plans."}{"title": "EQUIPO DE NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA Y DIET\u00c9TICA (UNCYD):The UNCyD team is responsible for assessing and monitoring the nutritional status of patients, ensuring appropriate dietary interventions are implemented."}{"title": "TEST DE VOLUMEN-VISCOSIDAD:The volume-viscosity test is a clinical evaluation performed by nursing staff to assess the swallowing capabilities of patients."}{"title": "ENDOCINOLOG\u00cdA:The Endocrinolog\u00eda (Endocrinology) service deals with hormonal and metabolic disorders, which can impact nutritional status and swallowing."}{"title": "CONSULTA PRIMERA DISFAGIA OROFAR\u00cdNGEA:The Consulta Primera Disfagia Orofar\u00edngea is a specialized consultation for the initial assessment of patients suspected of having oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "VIDEOFLOUROSCOPIAS:Videofluoroscopias are diagnostic procedures performed to assess swallowing function in patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "MUST:The Malnutrition Universal Screening Tool (MUST) is a comprehensive screening tool designed to identify adults at risk of malnutrition. It is recommended by the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN) for use in community settings and various healthcare environments. MUST serves as a valuable resource for assessing nutritional risk in the general population, helping healthcare professionals to identify individuals who may be malnourished or at risk of malnutrition. This tool is particularly effective in screening patients and community members, facilitating early intervention and management of malnutrition. Overall, MUST is recognized as an essential instrument for evaluating nutritional status and addressing malnutrition risk among adults."}{"title": "MNA S-F:The Mini Nutritional Assessment Short-Form (MNA S-F) is a tool used to evaluate the nutritional status of elderly patients."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS SEGUROS:The safe foods provided by the Servicio de Cocina Hospitalaria for the evaluation of dysphagia include yogurt and custard."}{"title": "ALIMENTOS PELIGROSOS:\"ALIMENTOS PELIGROSOS\" refers to foods that pose significant risks for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. These dangerous foods include sticky items and those that can easily fragment, which may lead to choking or aspiration. Specifically, the foods identified as hazardous for individuals undergoing dysphagia assessment encompass orange, noodle soup, croquettes, meatballs in sauce, toasted bread, and cookies. It is crucial for caregivers and healthcare providers to be aware of these foods to ensure the safety and well-being of patients with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "UNIDAD DE LOGOPEDIA:The Unidad de Logopedia (Speech Therapy Unit) provides rehabilitative treatment for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "FISIOTERAPIA:The Fisioterapia (Physiotherapy) service may be involved in the rehabilitation of patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "ALZHEIMER:Alzheimer's disease is a progressive neurodegenerative disorder that primarily affects memory and cognitive function, leading to significant cognitive decline. It is characterized by the presence of beta-amyloid plaques in the brain and the degeneration of brain cells. This condition not only impacts the patient's ability to perform daily activities but also contributes to complications such as dysphagia and malnutrition. Various risk factors are associated with Alzheimer's disease, including cardiovascular disease, diabetes mellitus, and elevated levels of homocysteine. Additionally, dietary habits may influence the progression of the disease. Overall, Alzheimer's disease represents a serious neurological condition that poses challenges for both patients and caregivers."}{"title": "CUESTIONARIOS DE SATISFACCI\u00d3N:Satisfaction questionnaires are tools used to evaluate patient satisfaction with care and services received, helping to identify areas for improvement in healthcare delivery."}{"title": "GRD:"}{"title": "KATIA SEVILLA:Katia Sevilla is a professional involved in interdisciplinary interventions related to dysphagia management."}{"title": "EIICHI SAITOH:Eiichi Saitoh is a researcher who contributed to the development of trans-disciplinary approaches for dysphagia rehabilitation in Japan."}{"title": "KOICHIRO MATSUNO:Koichiro Matsuno is a researcher involved in dysphagia rehabilitation studies in Japan."}{"title": "YOKO INAMOTO:Yoko Inamoto is a researcher who has worked on dysphagia rehabilitation in Japan."}{"title": "MAKOTO ISHIKAWA:Makoto Ishikawa is a researcher contributing to dysphagia rehabilitation approaches in Japan."}{"title": "AKIO TSUBAHARA:Akio Tsubahara is a researcher involved in the development of dysphagia rehabilitation methods in Japan."}{"title": "QASC TRIALISTS GROUP:The QASC Trialists Group is involved in implementing evidence-based treatment protocols for managing swallowing dysfunction in acute stroke patients."}{"title": "GESTI\u00d3N DEL CENTRO:Gesti\u00f3n del centro refers to the management practices within healthcare facilities that impact patient care and quality indicators."}{"title": "INDICADORES DE CALIDAD:\"INDICADORES DE CALIDAD\" refers to metrics utilized to evaluate the quality of care delivered in healthcare environments. These indicators are particularly significant in the context of dysphagia management, as they help ensure that patients receive appropriate and effective care. Overall, \"indicadores de calidad\" serve as essential tools for assessing the quality of healthcare services and patient care across various medical settings."}{"title": "DIETAS DE F\u00c1CIL DEGLUCI\u00d3N:Dietas de f\u00e1cil degluci\u00f3n are specialized diets designed for patients with swallowing difficulties, ensuring safe and adequate nutrition."}{"title": "CUIDADO Y ATENCI\u00d3N SANITARIA:Cuidado y atenci\u00f3n sanitaria refers to the overall healthcare services provided to patients, including those with dysphagia."}{"title": "EVIDENCIA-BASED TREATMENT PROTOCOLS:Evidencia-based treatment protocols are standardized methods used to manage dysphagia and improve patient outcomes.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "INTERNET:The Internet is a global network that facilitates instant communication and access to information across vast distances. It has revolutionized the way people connect and share data, transforming various aspects of daily life, business, and social interaction."}{"title": "DIGITAL TECHNOLOGY:Digital technology encompasses various tools and systems that enhance communication, information access, and health services, significantly impacting society."}{"title": "EHEALTH:eHealth refers to the use of digital technology and information and communication technologies to improve health services and patient care. It integrates various health information systems to enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of healthcare delivery, ultimately aiming to provide better health outcomes for patients."}{"title": "MHEALTH:MHEALTH, or Mobile Health, refers to the utilization of mobile devices and applications to enhance health services and information, particularly in the realms of patient care and health monitoring. It is a subset of eHealth, focusing on the integration of mobile technology to support health services. MHEALTH plays a significant role in improving patient engagement and is particularly effective in managing chronic diseases, thereby facilitating better health outcomes through continuous monitoring and support."}{"title": "TRHLAB:TRHLab is a tele-rehabilitation project developed at Hospital San Pau in Barcelona, specifically designed to address the needs of patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia. Led by Dr. Helena Bascu\u00f1ana, TRHLab utilizes digital tools to enhance education and training for both patients and healthcare providers. This initiative represents a significant opportunity for the advancement of digital technology in the field of dysphagia within Spain, aiming to improve patient outcomes through innovative management strategies."}{"title": "TELECOMUNICACIONES:Telecommunications encompasses the technologies and services that enable communication over distances, playing a vital role in the accessibility of digital health solutions."}{"title": "UNI\u00d3N INTERNACIONAL DE TELECOMUNICACIONES:The Uni\u00f3n Internacional de Telecomunicaciones (UIT) is a specialized agency of the United Nations that plays a crucial role in coordinating global telecommunication standards and policies. It is responsible for managing the global use of the radio-frequency spectrum and satellite orbits, ensuring that these resources are utilized efficiently and effectively. Additionally, the UIT develops technical standards for telecommunications, including significant recommendations such as UIT-T Y.3600, which pertains to big data. Through its various functions, the UIT aims to facilitate international cooperation in the field of telecommunications and promote the development of communication technologies worldwide."}{"title": "INFORME ONTSI:The ONTSI report provides statistical data on internet access and usage in Spain, highlighting trends in digital technology adoption."}{"title": "HOGARES ESPA\u00d1OLES:Spanish households are increasingly gaining access to the internet and mobile services, reflecting the growth of digital technology in the region."}{"title": "SALUD:SALUD refers to the overall condition of a person's body or mind, encompassing the presence or absence of illness or injury. This concept is significantly influenced by digital technology, which impacts various aspects of health, including patient care, research, and health promotion. Additionally, general health can be affected by conditions such as kidney stones and their complications, as well as associated conditions like diabetes and hypertension."}{"title": "NACIONES UNIDAS:Naciones Unidas, also known as the United Nations (UN), is an international organization founded in 1945 with the primary aim of promoting peace, security, and cooperation among countries. It plays a crucial role in addressing global issues, including the promotion of human rights, which encompasses matters related to gender identity. Additionally, the United Nations sets important guidelines on various topics, including food labeling standards, thereby contributing to international standards and practices. Through its multifaceted initiatives, Naciones Unidas strives to foster a more just and equitable world."}{"title": "MARTIN HILBERT:Martin Hilbert is a technology advisor at the Library of Congress in the United States and a professor at the University of California, known for his insights on digital information."}{"title": "TIM KELSEY:Tim Kelsey is the Executive Director of the Australian Digital Health Agency and has previously served as the Director of Patient Care and Information for the NHS."}{"title": "AGENCIA DE SALUD DIGITAL AUSTRALIANA:The Australian Digital Health Agency is responsible for digital health initiatives in Australia, aiming to improve health outcomes through technology."}{"title": "NHS:The National Health Service (NHS) is the publicly funded healthcare system in the United Kingdom, providing healthcare services to residents."}{"title": "AETSA:The Agency for Health Technology Assessment of Andalusia (AETSA) is a prominent organization dedicated to the evaluation of health technologies. It is recognized as a pioneer within the Spanish Network of Agencies for Health Technology Assessment, establishing itself as a leader in the field. AETSA plays a crucial role in assessing health technologies, contributing to informed decision-making in healthcare within the region of Andalusia."}{"title": "TECNOLOG\u00cdAS DE LA INFORMACI\u00d3N Y DE LA COMUNICACI\u00d3N:Information and Communication Technologies (ICT) encompass all technologies used to handle telecommunications, broadcast media, intelligent building management systems, and audio-visual processing and transmission systems."}{"title": "DIABETES:Diabetes is a chronic health condition characterized by high blood sugar levels, which significantly impacts how the body processes glucose. It often requires careful nutritional management and specific dietary protocols to control blood sugar levels and prevent complications. This condition is frequently associated with obesity, metabolic syndrome, and various health complications, including cardiovascular disease, kidney stone formation, and pancreatic cancer. \n\nDiabetes can manifest in different forms, including Type 1, Type 2, gestational diabetes, and MODY, and is a significant area of research and clinical focus, particularly regarding its treatment and management strategies. Patients with diabetes may require specialized dietary formulas designed to modify disease progression and manage their condition effectively. \n\nThe management of diabetes often involves medication, lifestyle changes, and adherence to specific dietary guidelines, such as those influenced by the Mediterranean diet. Additionally, diabetes can complicate the management of other health conditions, such as chronic kidney disease and obesity, and is linked to increased risks of frailty in older adults. \n\nIn some cases, diabetes may arise from hormonal imbalances or be a complication of other metabolic disorders, such as hereditary hemochromatosis or MELAS syndrome. The condition is also noted for its economic impact on healthcare systems and the importance of dietary assessment for prevention and treatment. Overall, diabetes is a complex metabolic disorder that requires comprehensive management to mitigate its effects on health and quality of life."}{"title": "OBESIDAD:Obesidad, or obesity, is a medical condition characterized by an excessive accumulation of body fat, which significantly increases the risk of various health issues, including hypertension, diabetes, cardiovascular diseases, and metabolic disorders. The prevalence of obesity has escalated dramatically on a global scale, rising from 105 million to 641 million individuals over the past four decades. This condition complicates nutritional assessments, particularly in children and critically ill patients, and is influenced by dietary habits, including the consumption of high-calorie foods, red and processed meats, sugar-sweetened beverages, and low fiber intake.\n\nObesidad can be managed through various interventions, including dietary modifications, increased protein intake, physical activity, and pharmacological treatments such as liraglutide. Additionally, surgical options like bariatric surgery are available for severe cases. The Mediterranean diet has shown beneficial effects in weight reduction, while adherence to healthy lifestyle habits is emphasized in programs like THAO-SALUD INFANTIL aimed at addressing obesity in children.\n\nThe condition is also linked to hormonal imbalances, as it can affect levels of sex hormone-binding globulin (SHBG) and aldosterone, and is associated with increased inflammation and chronic health complications. Obesidad is particularly concerning in older adults, where it can lead to sarcopenic obesity and increased fragility. Furthermore, it has been associated with kidney stones, hyperuricemia, and alterations in gut health and microbiome balance.\n\nOverall, obesity is a complex and multifaceted health issue that requires comprehensive management strategies, including dietary recommendations, lifestyle changes, and medical interventions, to mitigate its impact on individual and public health."}{"title": "IGNACIO HERN\u00c1NDEZ MEDRANO:Ignacio Hern\u00e1ndez Medrano is a Spanish neurologist known for developing the Savana program, which utilizes artificial intelligence to extract data from clinical histories."}{"title": "OMS:The OMS (Organizaci\u00f3n Mundial de la Salud), known in English as the World Health Organization (WHO), is a specialized agency of the United Nations responsible for coordinating international public health efforts. The OMS plays a crucial role in establishing health standards, providing guidelines, and conducting research on various health-related topics. It is involved in the classification of diseases, including specific conditions such as craniofaringiomas and neuroendocrine tumors, and has updated its classifications, notably in 2017 for pituitary tumors.\n\nThe OMS provides comprehensive guidelines on a wide range of health issues, including the management of acute diarrhea, nutritional needs, and dietary recommendations. It emphasizes the importance of proper nutrition for children, pregnant women, and lactating mothers, advocating for a varied diet that meets all necessary nutrient requirements. The organization also offers formulas for estimating energy expenditure and dietary needs, which are essential for understanding the nutritional status of different populations.\n\nIn addition to its focus on nutrition, the OMS addresses broader health topics such as active aging, telemedicine, and the use of information and communication technologies in healthcare. It provides guidelines for rehydration solutions and has developed international reference patterns for child growth, contributing to global health initiatives aimed at improving the quality of life.\n\nThe OMS is recognized for its leadership in global health matters, shaping the health research agenda, and providing critical data on health issues such as diabetes prevalence and obesity management. Through its extensive guidelines and recommendations, the OMS aims to optimize health opportunities and enhance the overall well-being of populations worldwide."}{"title": "BIG DATA:Big Data refers to the large volumes of data that can be collected, stored, managed, analyzed, and visualized in real-time. It plays a crucial role in improving health interventions and patient care by enabling the analysis of extensive datasets. In the context of health data, Big Data facilitates the extraction of valuable insights that can enhance decision-making and optimize healthcare outcomes."}{"title": "SAVANA:Savana is a pioneering project developed in Spain that focuses on the application of artificial intelligence in healthcare. Currently operational in numerous care centers, Savana aims to enhance the usability of clinical data. The program, created by Ignacio Hern\u00e1ndez Medrano, utilizes artificial intelligence to transform unstructured clinical data into valuable information, thereby improving healthcare delivery and decision-making processes."}{"title": "HISTORIA CL\u00cdNICA ELECTR\u00d3NICA:The \"HISTORIA CL\u00cdNICA ELECTR\u00d3NICA\" (HCE) is an electronic health record system designed to store and manage comprehensive patient data. It includes the nutritional and medical history of patients, facilitating their ongoing monitoring and care. The HCE plays a crucial role in managing health conditions by providing vital information that supports healthcare professionals in making informed decisions regarding patient treatment and follow-up."}{"title": "DISPOSITIVOS TECNOL\u00d3GICOS:Technological devices, such as wearables, are designed to monitor health parameters and collect data relevant to patient care and management."}{"title": "TELEMEDICINA:Telemedicine is the practice of providing healthcare services remotely using telecommunications technology, facilitating diagnosis, treatment, and patient management from a distance."}{"title": "HOSPITAL SAN PAU:Hospital San Pau in Barcelona is a prominent healthcare institution that has been actively involved in telemedicine since 2010. It has developed a specialized initiative known as TRHLab, which focuses on the rehabilitation of oropharyngeal dysphagia. In addition to this initiative, Hospital San Pau provides valuable resources for both patients and healthcare professionals concerning dysphagia, further emphasizing its commitment to improving patient care and rehabilitation through innovative medical practices."}{"title": "DRA. HELENA BASCU\u00d1ANA:Dr. Helena Bascu\u00f1ana is a medical professional who is currently leading the TRHLab project at Hospital San Pau, where she focuses on tele-rehabilitation for patients suffering from dysphagia. In addition to her work in tele-rehabilitation, Dr. Bascu\u00f1ana has also created valuable video content on dysphagia, which is available on YouTube, further contributing to the awareness and understanding of this condition."}{"title": "HOSPITAL SON ESPASES:Hospital Son Espases is a medical facility that offers an app and web resources for patients dealing with dysphagia."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO MIGUEL SERVET:Hospital Universitario Miguel Servet is a prominent healthcare institution located in Zaragoza, Spain. It specializes in clinical nutrition and dietetics, with a particular focus on providing services for diabetic patients. The hospital is led by Dr. Alejandro Sanz Par\u00eds, who heads the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit. Additionally, the institution offers resources for dysphagia management through the Disfapp app. Another notable professional associated with the hospital is Diego \u00c1lvarez Ballano. Overall, Hospital Universitario Miguel Servet is recognized for its comprehensive approach to nutrition and endocrinology, making it a key player in the healthcare landscape of Zaragoza."}{"title": "FRESENIUS KABI:Fresenius Kabi is a global healthcare company that specializes in lifesaving medicines and technologies. The company focuses on a range of products, including nutritional solutions and medical devices. Fresenius Kabi is particularly known for its nutritional products, such as Fresubin, Supportan Drink, Diben est\u00e1ndar, Diben Drink, and Fresubin HP Energy, which cater to various dietary needs, including enteral nutrition and parenteral nutrition. The company also produces solutions and additives for medical use, specifically designed for managing dysphagia and supporting patients requiring specialized nutritional care. Through its commitment to innovation and collaboration with healthcare institutions, Fresenius Kabi plays a vital role in enhancing patient care and outcomes in the healthcare sector."}{"title": "NESTL\u00c9:Nestl\u00e9 is a global multinational food and beverage company renowned for its extensive range of nutritional products and solutions. The company provides resources for managing dysphagia through its health management website and is recognized for its specialized nutritional offerings, including enteral formulas and products tailored for children and patients with specific dietary needs. Among its notable products are Novasource, Resource Diabet, Resource Peptide, Resource Diabet Plus, and various nutritional drinks such as Renutryl and Resource 2.0.\n\nNestl\u00e9 also produces a variety of nutritional supplements, including Isosource Protein, Isosource Mix, Resource Support Plus, and Impact Enteral, catering to diverse dietary requirements. The company is committed to supporting health management through dietary software like Dietsource\u00ae and has a strong focus on infant nutrition and milk fortifiers. Additionally, Nestl\u00e9 has been involved in the development of the Mini Nutritional Assessment (MNA), first published in 1994 and revised in 2006, further emphasizing its dedication to nutritional health. Overall, Nestl\u00e9 stands out as a leader in the food and beverage industry, particularly in the realm of nutritional products."}{"title": "VEGENAT:VEGENAT is a company dedicated to the nutrition and feeding of elderly individuals, actively sponsoring the series \"Envejecimiento y Nutrici\u00f3n.\" In 2014, VEGENAT produced documents focused on ideal diets for the elderly and nutritional interventions for fragile elderly individuals. The brand is associated with health and nutrition, as indicated by its logo and collaborative efforts. VEGENAT specializes in plant-based nutritional products, offering dietary supplements tailored to specific health needs, including solutions for dysphagia. The company manufactures a variety of dietary products, such as TDiET HP, TDiET HP sin fibra, T-Diet PLUS for diabetic patients, Diaba HP, TDiET 2, T-DIET Energy, At\u00e9mpero Enteral, Dienat G, and Suppresi. Overall, VEGENAT is committed to providing high-calorie and plant-based nutritional solutions, collaborating with healthcare institutions to enhance the well-being of its consumers."}{"title": "NUTRICIA:Nutricia is a specialized nutrition company that is part of the Danone Group, focusing on medical nutrition and dietary products. The brand is known for producing a wide range of nutritional products, including arginine supplements, enteral formulas, and specialized nutritional formulas for infants and children. Nutricia's product offerings include Nutrison Protein Plus, Nutrison Protein Plus Energy, Nutrison Multifibre, and Nutrison Advanced Cubison, among others. \n\nThe company develops products aimed at providing nutritional support for various medical needs, including energy supplementation for patients requiring additional caloric intake, as exemplified by their Infatrini\u00ae formula. Nutricia also addresses specific dietary requirements for individuals with metabolic disorders, such as phenylketonuria, and offers resources for patients with dysphagia. \n\nIn addition to their focus on pediatric nutrition, Nutricia provides dietary management solutions for adults, including products like Fortimel Complete, Fortimel Extra, and Forticare. Their commitment to specialized nutrition is evident in their extensive range of medical nutrition products designed to meet the unique needs of patients across different health conditions. Overall, Nutricia is dedicated to advancing medical nutrition and providing tailored dietary solutions for individuals with specific nutritional requirements."}{"title": "SEMI:SEMI is an organization that provides information and resources for patients dealing with dysphagia."}{"title": "MOODLE:Moodle is a widely used online learning platform designed for educational purposes, facilitating various forms of online training and courses. It is particularly effective for structured training programs, including those in biomedical education."}{"title": "FUTURE LEARN:Future Learn is an online learning platform that provides a diverse range of courses and educational resources, making it a popular choice in the field of online education. The platform offers various training programs, including those specifically focused on health education, catering to a wide audience seeking to enhance their knowledge and skills through accessible online learning opportunities."}{"title": "DR. GOOGLE:Dr. Google is a colloquial term referring to the practice of searching for medical information online, often leading to misinformation."}{"title": "TRH LAB:TRH Lab is a telemedicine platform that provides resources and information for patients and professionals regarding dysphagia."}{"title": "DYSFAGIAWEB:DysfagiaWeb is an online platform that offers information and resources for patients dealing with dysphagia."}{"title": "DYSFAPP:Dysfapp is an application designed to assist patients and professionals in managing dysphagia."}{"title": "OSAKIDETZA:Osakidetza is the health service of the Basque Country that provides resources for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "DISFAGIA NUTRICION:Disfagia Nutricion is an organization that offers nutritional resources for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "DISFAGIA SOLUCION:Disfagia Solucion is an organization that provides solutions and resources for managing dysphagia."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD ESPA\u00d1OLA DE ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:The \"Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n\" (SEEN) is a prominent professional organization based in Spain, dedicated to the study, research, and treatment of endocrine and nutritional disorders. It plays a crucial role in the dissemination of knowledge in these fields, having published various guidelines, manuals, and educational resources, including the \"Manual de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n.\" \n\nSEEN is involved in the research and education of endocrinology and nutrition, providing valuable resources for the evaluation and management of various conditions, such as dislipemias, metabolic bone disease associated with home parenteral nutrition, hyperprolactinemia, and multiple endocrine neoplasia. The organization also offers online video courses and other educational materials to support training in these areas.\n\nAs a scientific society, SEEN is committed to promoting the advancement of endocrinology and nutrition in Spain, and it supports the professional development of its members, including notable figures such as Nuria Valdes Gallego, who has been actively involved in the Neuroendocrinology and Thyroid Area and served on the board from 2008 to 2011. Overall, the Sociedad Espa\u00f1ola de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n is a vital institution for healthcare professionals in Spain, fostering research, education, and best practices in the fields of endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "DYSHPHAGIA THERAPY:Dysphagia Therapy is a mobile application designed to assist medical professionals in evaluating swallowing disorders and determining appropriate rehabilitation options."}{"title": "REDES SOCIALES:REDES SOCIALES, or social networks, are platforms that facilitate social interaction and information sharing among users. They play a significant role in health communication, providing a space for users to connect and exchange information. However, despite their potential, social networks currently exhibit minimal engagement with content related to dysphagia, indicating a gap in the dissemination and discussion of this specific health topic within these platforms."}{"title": "GAMIFICACI\u00d3N:Gamification is the application of game-design elements in non-game contexts, aimed at enhancing engagement and learning in various fields, including healthcare education."}{"title": "TIC:TIC, or Information and Communication Technologies, refers to a range of digital tools and resources designed to enhance communication and information sharing, especially within the healthcare sector. These technologies play a crucial role in improving the efficiency and effectiveness of healthcare delivery by enabling better access to information and facilitating interactions among healthcare providers and patients."}{"title": "TABACO:TABACO refers to tobacco, a substance that is widely recognized for its negative health impacts. It is strongly advised to avoid tobacco consumption for at least 12 hours prior to medical tests to ensure accurate results, particularly in imaging procedures. The use of tobacco is discouraged due to its detrimental effects on bone health, as it is a known risk factor for osteoporosis. This is especially critical for patients with obesity and those undergoing bariatric surgery, as tobacco can exacerbate health complications in these groups. Furthermore, tobacco smoking has been established as a significant risk factor for the development of Graves' disease, with studies indicating an odds ratio of 3.5. Overall, tobacco consumption is a major public health concern, and health promotion programs often focus on reducing smoking rates to improve overall health outcomes."}{"title": "FORMACI\u00d3N BIOM\u00c9DICA:"}{"title": "CRISTINA TEJERA:Cristina Tejera is a specialist in Endocrinology and Nutrition, recognized as a prominent ambassador for her specialty on social media, with over 5,000 followers on Twitter as of April 2018."}{"title": "TWITTER:Twitter is a social media platform that allows global interaction and information sharing, particularly popular among health professionals and the general public."}{"title": "FACEBOOK:Facebook is a global social media platform that enables users to create groups for sharing information, making it particularly popular among patients. Within this platform, various profiles related to dysphagia can be found, encompassing both professional services and personal accounts. This diverse range of content allows users to connect, share experiences, and access resources related to dysphagia, highlighting Facebook's role as a significant tool for community engagement and information dissemination in health-related contexts."}{"title": "INSTAGRAM:Instagram is a social media platform focused on image sharing, used in the health sector for education and information dissemination."}{"title": "LINKEDIN:LinkedIn is a professional networking site and social media platform that facilitates connections and content sharing among professionals across various sectors. Within this platform, groups related to dysphagia have been identified, primarily consisting of individual profiles. This highlights LinkedIn's role not only as a networking tool but also as a space for specialized discussions and connections within specific fields."}{"title": "YOUTUBE:YouTube is a video-sharing platform that serves as a valuable tool for information dissemination and professional training across various fields, including health. It hosts numerous publications on dysphagia, featuring content from professionals that provides essential insights and knowledge on the subject."}{"title": "DRA. BASCU\u00d1ANA:Dr. Bascu\u00f1ana is a professional involved in the TRHlab project, focusing on oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "FUNDACI\u00d3N SIN \u00c1NIMO DE LUCRO:A non-profit foundation focused on fighting dysphagia, involved in raising awareness and providing support for affected individuals."}{"title": "AGRUPACI\u00d3N ARGENTINA:An Argentine group that aims to raise awareness about progressive supranuclear palsy, which may include issues related to dysphagia."}{"title": "DA\u00d1O CEREBRAL:"}{"title": "TELEASISTENCIA:Teleassistance refers to the medical assistance provided remotely, optimizing resources for healthcare systems and patients."}{"title": "M\u00c9XICO:Mexico is another Latin American country where many profiles related to dysphagia were identified on social media."}{"title": "PACIENTE CON DISFAGIA:A patient with dysphagia who shared culinary tools on social media, highlighting personal experiences with the condition."}{"title": "BRASIL:Brasil es un pa\u00eds que proporciona datos sobre el crecimiento infantil y la nutrici\u00f3n en el contexto de la Organizaci\u00f3n Mundial de la Salud (OMS)."}{"title": "FUNDACI\u00d3N ISYS:The FUNDACI\u00d3N ISYS is a foundation dedicated to the evaluation of internet content and health technologies, with a particular focus on dysphagia. In addition to its work in this area, the iSYS Foundation also assesses health mobile applications, utilizing objective variables to inform users about the popularity, trustworthiness, and utility of these applications. Through its comprehensive evaluations, FUNDACI\u00d3N ISYS aims to enhance the quality and reliability of health-related digital resources."}{"title": "DISCERN:Discern is an international tool that helps users distinguish between more or less reliable health content through a questionnaire."}{"title": "MIGUEL \u00c1NGEL M\u00c1\u00d1EZ:Miguel \u00c1ngel M\u00e1\u00f1ez is a commentator who discusses the challenges of accreditation in health content and the importance of professional recommendations."}{"title": "WEB NO BASADAS EN LA EVIDENCIA:Webs Not Based on Evidence (WNBE) refers to unreliable health websites that users should avoid visiting."}{"title": "DATOS PERSONALES:Personal data refers to sensitive information used in mobile applications, wearables, and electronic health records, which has significant potential for companies and research."}{"title": "NOMOFOBIA:Nomophobia is the irrational fear of being without a mobile phone, highlighting the psychological impact of technology on individuals."}{"title": "WHATSAPPITIS:Whatsappitis is a condition resulting from excessive use of mobile messaging, characterized by inflammation and discomfort in the hand or wrist."}{"title": "POSVERDAD:Post-truth refers to the phenomenon where information is manipulated to influence public opinion and emotions, often seen in the context of social media."}{"title": "DIOGENES INFORM\u00c1TICO:Digital Diogenes describes the overwhelming amount of data and content that individuals struggle to organize or utilize effectively."}{"title": "REALIDAD VIRTUAL:Virtual reality is a technology that has become a strong ally in the rehabilitation of patients with brain damage, and it may also play a significant role in the treatment of dysphagia."}{"title": "PHOTOVOICE:Photovoice is a qualitative research methodology based on community participation that aims to give voice to socially marginalized groups through photography."}{"title": "INTERNET DE LAS COSAS:The Internet of Things (IoT) refers to the interconnection of objects via the internet, which can significantly impact daily life and work by automating tasks."}{"title": "WEARABLES:Wearables are devices that can be worn on the body, which, along with biosensors, are expected to increase the availability of health data exponentially."}{"title": "INTELIGENCIA ARTIFICIAL:Artificial intelligence is a rapidly advancing technology that is expected to play a crucial role in healthcare decision-making and patient management."}{"title": "BIOSENSORES:Biosensors are devices that can detect biological changes and are integral to the development of wearable health technology."}{"title": "CUIDADOS:CUIDADOS refers to the various methods and practices aimed at promoting health and well-being. This concept encompasses a range of approaches that can be enhanced through the use of technology, indicating a modern integration of care practices with technological advancements to improve overall health outcomes."}{"title": "TECNOLOG\u00cdA DIGITAL:"}{"title": "ONTSI:ONTSI is an organization under Red.es, part of the Ministry of Energy, Tourism and Digital Agency in Spain, focusing on telecommunications and information society studies."}{"title": "RED.ES:Red.es is a public business entity that promotes the digital economy and the use of information and communication technologies in Spain."}{"title": "MINISTERIO DE ENERG\u00cdA, TURISMO Y AGENCIA DIGITAL:The Ministry of Energy, Tourism and Digital Agency is a governmental body in Spain responsible for energy, tourism, and digital transformation policies."}{"title": "FUNDACI\u00d3N VODAFONE ESPA\u00d1A:Fundaci\u00f3n Vodafone Espa\u00f1a is a foundation that focuses on social projects and initiatives related to technology and digital inclusion in Spain."}{"title": "ANDALUC\u00cdA:Andaluc\u00eda is an autonomous community located in the southern part of Spain, recognized for its rich cultural heritage and significant healthcare initiatives. It is home to the Agencia de Evaluaci\u00f3n de Tecnolog\u00edas Sanitarias, which plays a vital role in contributing to public health. The region faces challenges related to health, notably high obesity prevalence rates, which have prompted specific healthcare policies. For instance, patients in Andaluc\u00eda are required to submit a justification report to continue receiving treatment for their nutritional needs. Overall, Andaluc\u00eda combines a deep cultural legacy with ongoing efforts to address public health issues."}{"title": "SEVILLA:Sevilla is a city in Spain, serving as the capital of Andaluc\u00eda. It is renowned for its historical significance and is recognized as a center for health technology evaluation. Within this vibrant city, Fernando Garc\u00eda P\u00e9rez-Sevillano practices, contributing to the local health landscape."}{"title": "UNIVERSIDAD AUT\u00d3NOMA DE BARCELONA:The Universidad Aut\u00f3noma de Barcelona is a public university located in Spain, known for its commitment to research and education across various fields, including medicine. It is an esteemed educational institution where Ana M.\u00aa Urioste Fondo completed her Master's in Research Methodology. Additionally, it is the alma mater of Miguel A. Rubio Herrera, who obtained his medical degree from the university in 1982."}{"title": "GABRIELA C.:Gabriela C. is a researcher who designed a mobile health app for patients with dysphagia following head and neck cancer."}{"title": "BASCUNANA H.:Bascu\u00f1ana H. is a researcher who has worked on tele-rehabilitation for oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "MEDRANO MH:Medrano MH is associated with Savana, a company focused on health technology solutions."}{"title": "CHARNKOCK D.:Charnkock D. is an author involved in the development of the DISCERN Handbook, which evaluates health information quality."}{"title": "DISCERN HANDBOOK:"}{"title": "TELE-REHABILITACI\u00d3N:Tele-rehabilitation refers to the use of technology to provide rehabilitation services remotely, particularly for patients with swallowing disorders."}{"title": "ENFERMEDADES RARAS:ENFERMEDADES RARAS refers to rare diseases, which are conditions that affect a small percentage of the population and often necessitate specialized medical attention and support. In Spain, the CIBERer is a dedicated research center focused on these rare diseases, aiming to advance understanding and treatment options for affected individuals."}{"title": "CUIDADO DE LA SALUD:CUIDADO DE LA SALUD refers to the essential aspect of healthcare, particularly in the context of providing medical services to individuals, including those who are incarcerated and may be on hunger strikes. It encompasses the organized provision of medical services aimed at maintaining or improving health. This highlights the critical importance of health care in ensuring the well-being of vulnerable populations, emphasizing the need for attentive and responsive health services in various circumstances."}{"title": "DIGITAL INCLUSION:Digital inclusion involves ensuring that all individuals have access to and can effectively use digital technologies."}{"title": "TECNOLOG\u00cdAS DE LA INFORMACI\u00d3N Y LA COMUNICACI\u00d3N:Information and Communication Technologies (ICT) encompass all technologies used to handle telecommunications, broadcast media, intelligent building management systems, audio-visual processing and transmission systems, and network-based control and monitoring functions."}{"title": "SOCIEDAD DE LA INFORMACI\u00d3N:The Information Society refers to a society where the creation, distribution, and manipulation of information is a significant economic, political, and cultural activity.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "EUROPEAN PUBLIC HEALTH ALLIANCE:The European Public Health Alliance is an organization focused on public health issues in Europe, including health inequalities and eHealth initiatives."}{"title": "ATHENS:Athens is the capital city of Greece, known for its historical significance and as a host for various international events, including the 2014 eHealth Forum."}{"title": "BMC PUBLIC HEALTH:BMC Public Health is a peer-reviewed journal dedicated to publishing research on a wide range of public health issues. The journal features studies that encompass various topics, including nutritional interventions for the elderly, general nutrition, and disease prevention. Additionally, BMC Public Health includes participatory action research projects, highlighting its commitment to diverse methodologies in addressing public health challenges. Through its comprehensive approach, the journal aims to contribute valuable insights and findings to the field of public health."}{"title": "HIGIENE BUCODENTAL:Higiene bucodental refers to the practices and protocols aimed at maintaining oral health and preventing infections, particularly in patients with limited autonomy and those with swallowing difficulties. These oral hygiene practices are critical for ensuring cleanliness and preventing complications during feeding, especially for patients with dysphagia. Maintaining proper oral hygiene is essential for overall health and well-being, as it helps to mitigate the risk of infections and other oral health issues."}{"title": "ENFERMERA:The enfermera, or nurse, is a vital healthcare professional dedicated to providing comprehensive patient care. Their responsibilities encompass monitoring patients' nutritional status and implementing postural techniques for those suffering from dysphagia. Additionally, the enfermera plays a crucial role in oral care, which includes assessing the mucosa and educating patients on the significance of maintaining good oral hygiene. Furthermore, the nurse is tasked with administering medications and overseeing patient care related to the functionality of catheters, ensuring that all aspects of patient health are effectively managed."}{"title": "TCAE:T\u00e9cnico de Cuidados Auxiliares de Enfermer\u00eda (TCAE) assists the enfermera in providing oral care to patients."}{"title": "PROCEDIMIENTO EN PACIENTES AUT\u00d3NOMOS:This procedure outlines the steps for providing oral hygiene care to patients who are autonomous."}{"title": "PROCEDIMIENTO EN PACIENTE CONSCIENTE CON AUTONOM\u00cdA LIMITADA:This procedure describes how to provide oral hygiene care to patients who are conscious but have limited autonomy."}{"title": "PACIENTE CON BAJO NIVEL DE CONSCIENCIA:This procedure details the steps for providing oral care to patients with a low level of consciousness."}{"title": "PACIENTE CON RESPIRACI\u00d3N MEC\u00c1NICA ASISTIDA:This procedure outlines the oral care steps for patients who are on mechanical ventilation."}{"title": "MUCOSA:Mucosa refers to the mucous membrane lining the oral cavity, which is assessed during oral care."}{"title": "CEPIJO DE DIENTES:Cepillo de dientes is a tool used in the practice of oral hygiene to clean teeth."}{"title": "CREMA DENT\u00cdFRICA:Crema dent\u00edfrica is toothpaste used in conjunction with a toothbrush for effective oral hygiene."}{"title": "LIMPIADOR DE LENGUA:Limpiador de lengua is a tool used to clean the tongue as part of oral hygiene practices."}{"title": "COLUTORIO:Colutorio is a mouthwash used to rinse the mouth and enhance oral hygiene."}{"title": "SUERO FISIOL\u00d3GICO:Suero fisiol\u00f3gico is a saline solution that may be used in oral care procedures."}{"title": "GASAS NO EST\u00c9RILES:Gasas no est\u00e9riles are non-sterile gauze used in various oral care procedures."}{"title": "DEPRESOR LINGUAL:Depresor lingual is a tongue depressor used to help access the oral cavity during care."}{"title": "VASELINA:Vaselina is used to hydrate the lips and surrounding areas during oral care."}{"title": "ASPIRADOR:Aspirador is a suction device used to remove secretions from the oral cavity."}{"title": "SONDAS DE ASPIRACI\u00d3N:Sondas de aspiraci\u00f3n are suction tubes used in oral care to clear secretions."}{"title": "GUANTES NO EST\u00c9RILES:Guantes no est\u00e9riles are non-sterile gloves worn during oral hygiene procedures."}{"title": "BATEA:Batea is a basin used to collect fluids during oral hygiene practices."}{"title": "TOALLA:Toalla is a towel used to keep the area clean during oral care."}{"title": "EMPAPADOR:Empapador is an absorbent pad used to protect surfaces during oral hygiene procedures."}{"title": "CAVIDAD BUCAL:"}{"title": "CUIDADOS EN LA ALIMENTACI\u00d3N DEL PACIENTE CON DISFAGIA OROFAR\u00cdNGEA:This document outlines the nursing care protocols for feeding patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "MANUAL DE DISFAGIA OROFAR\u00cdNGEA: SOLUCIONES MULTIDISCIPLINARES:This manual provides multidisciplinary solutions and guidelines for managing patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "ESTRATEGIAS POSTURALES:Postural strategies that modify the dimensions of the oropharynx and digestive tract to improve swallowing safety for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "FIGURA 2:FIGURA 2 serves as a comprehensive illustration that encompasses multiple aspects of clinical nutrition. It depicts the action of a homogenizer in the preparation of clinical nutrition products, emphasizing the importance of this equipment in ensuring the consistency and quality of nutritional formulations. Additionally, FIGURA 2 highlights the position of the caregiver while feeding a patient, underscoring the caregiver's critical role in implementing proper feeding techniques to enhance patient care. Furthermore, the figure illustrates the process of detecting and managing elevated gastric residuals in patients receiving enteral nutrition, which is essential for monitoring patient safety and nutritional efficacy. Overall, FIGURA 2 integrates these elements to provide a holistic view of the practices involved in clinical nutrition management."}{"title": "FIGURA 3:Figure 3 depicts the correct position for a patient who is bedridden during feeding, ensuring safety and comfort."}{"title": "RAQUEL G\u00d3MEZ RIVILLO:Raquel G\u00f3mez Rivillo is the illustrator for the manual on oropharyngeal dysphagia solutions, providing visual aids for the exercises described."}{"title": "EJERCICIOS OROFACIALES NO DEGLUTORIOS:Exercises aimed at improving orofacial structures and movements important for swallowing, without including the act of swallowing itself, as described in the manual."}{"title": "CUPA BLANCA:The white cup is used by an individual demonstrating the proper body position for safe drinking for those with oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "UTENSILIOS ADAPTATIVOS:Adaptive utensils designed to promote self-feeding, including a wide ergonomic handle utensil, a spoon with a curved handle, and a cup with a specialized spout or lid."}{"title": "JERINGAS DE ALIMENTACI\u00d3N:Medical syringes used for feeding, which are advised against for individuals with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "CUCHARAS DE VOLUMEN ALTO:Spoons with high volumes (>10 ml) that are recommended to be avoided for individuals with swallowing difficulties."}{"title": "CUIDADOS EN LA ALIMENTACI\u00d3N:Guidelines for the care of patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia, focusing on safe feeding practices."}{"title": "INTERVENCI\u00d3N:The systematic approach to treating orofacial musculature tailored to the specific needs of each patient."}{"title": "EJERCICIOS:Exercises aimed at improving the strength, speed, and synchronization of swallowing, as part of the treatment for dysphagia."}{"title": "VASO AZUL:"}{"title": "LABIOS-ESF\u00cdNTER LABIAL:Exercises designed to increase the muscle tone of the lips, focusing on their function as a sphincter."}{"title": "MUSCULATURA LINGUAL:Exercises aimed at enhancing the strength and endurance of the tongue muscles through resistance training."}{"title": "TERAPEUTA:A professional who guides patients through exercises to improve oral and facial muscle function."}{"title": "EJERCICIO LABIAL DEL BOT\u00d3N:An exercise involving a button placed between the lips to activate the orbicular muscle while the therapist applies tension."}{"title": "EJERCICIO DE MANTENIMIENTO DE PESAS LABIALES:An exercise where weights are held between the lips to strengthen lip muscles."}{"title": "EJERCICIOS DE POTENCIACI\u00d3N DE LA MUSCULATURA LINGUAL:Exercises designed to enhance the strength and endurance of the tongue muscles through resistance training."}{"title": "EJERCICIO CONTRA RESISTENCIA LINGUAL MANTENIDA Y FLUCTUANTE:An exercise where the tongue is extended against resistance provided by a therapist using a tongue depressor."}{"title": "EJERCICIO DE LA PAPADA:An exercise focusing on the contraction of the base of the tongue by applying pressure in a specific direction."}{"title": "EJERCICIOS PARA AUMENTAR EL TONO MUSCULAR DE LOS LABIOS-ESF\u00cdNTER LABIAL:"}{"title": "M\u00daSCULO MILOHIOIDEO:The milohyoid muscle is a muscle that plays a role in the movement of the tongue and is involved in swallowing."}{"title": "EJERCICIOS DE PESAS LINGUALES:The tongue weight exercises involve attaching a lead weight to a plastic washer, which the patient must hold with their tongue to build strength over time."}{"title": "PRESI\u00d3N M\u00c1XIMA:Maximum pressure refers to the highest force exerted by the tongue during exercises, used to tailor training programs for patients."}{"title": "SESIONES DE EJERCICIOS:Sessions of exercises are structured training periods aimed at improving the muscle tone and function of the tongue over a specified duration."}{"title": "CONTROL Y FEEDBACK VISUAL:Visual control and feedback are provided by the IOPI device to help patients understand their performance during tongue exercises."}{"title": "M\u00daSCULO LINGUAL:The lingual muscle is crucial for tongue movement and plays a significant role in swallowing and speech."}{"title": "EJERCICIO LINGUAL DEL BOT\u00d3N:"}{"title": "EJERCICIO DE SUCCI\u00d3N DE CHUPETE:An exercise aimed at improving the mobility of the buccinator muscle through suction against resistance using a pacifier."}{"title": "EJERCICIO DE SUCCI\u00d3N CON JERINGA:An exercise that involves sucking air from a syringe to enhance muscle control and strength in the mouth."}{"title": "EJERCICIO DE APERTURA MANDIBULAR:An exercise designed to balance the fascia and muscles that open the mouth, focusing on slow and controlled movements."}{"title": "EJERCICIO DE APERTURA MANDIBULAR CONTRA RESISTENCIA:An exercise that helps relax the muscles that close the mouth while strengthening the chewing muscles through gentle resistance."}{"title": "EJERCICIOS MANDIBULARES:Isotonic exercises designed to enhance the global and analytical movements of the temporomandibular joint and jaw."}{"title": "EJERCICIO CON GOMA TUBULAR:An exercise involving the use of tubular rubber to perform isometric contractions for jaw movement."}{"title": "EJERCICIOS PARA AUMENTAR EL TONO MUSCULAR DEL COMPLEJO BUCCINADOR:"}{"title": "EJERCICIO DE SHAKER:An exercise aimed at enhancing the isotonic and isometric strength of the suprahyoid muscles to improve the upper esophageal sphincter opening and reduce post-swallowing residue."}{"title": "VELO PALATINO:The soft palate, which is crucial for proper swallowing and preventing food from entering the nasal cavity."}{"title": "BUCCINADORES:Muscles of the cheek that help in holding the air in the mouth while performing certain exercises."}{"title": "FIGURA 16:An illustration series showing a person performing the Shaker exercise in various positions to enhance muscle strength."}{"title": "FIGURA 17:An illustration showing a person performing suction exercises, both with and without a straw, to strengthen the suprahyoid muscles."}{"title": "ESTIMULACI\u00d3N VIBRATORIA DEL VELO PALATINO:A specific exercise involving the use of a small micro-vibration device to stimulate the soft palate, enhancing its function in swallowing."}{"title": "EJERCICIO DEL GLOBO:An exercise that involves inflating a balloon using the mouth to improve muscle tone and mobility of the soft palate."}{"title": "EJERCICIOS DE SUELO DE BOCA:Exercises aimed at strengthening the suprahyoid muscles through suction techniques to enhance oral function."}{"title": "EJERCICIOS PARA AUMENTAR EL TONO Y MEJORAR LA MOVILIDAD DEL VELO PALATINO:"}{"title": "GU\u00cdA T\u00c9CNICA DE INTERVENCI\u00d3N LOGOP\u00c9DICA EN TERAPIA MIOFUNCIONAL:A technical guide on speech therapy intervention in myofunctional therapy, relevant to dysphagia treatment."}{"title": "TERAPIA MIOFUNCIONAL OROFACIAL:Orofacial myofunctional therapy is a treatment approach that may be relevant for patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "EFFECT OF TONGUE STRENGTH TRAINING:A study examining the impact of tongue strength training on swallowing in stroke patients, relevant to dysphagia."}{"title": "REHABILITATION OF SWALLOWING BY EXERCISE:Research focused on rehabilitating swallowing through exercise in patients with dysphagia."}{"title": "ESCALAS DE FUNCI\u00d3N Y CALIDAD DE VIDA EN DISFAGIA OROFAR\u00cdNGEA DEL ADULTO:Scales for assessing function and quality of life in adults with oropharyngeal dysphagia."}{"title": "BIBLIOGRAF\u00cdA:BIBLIOGRAF\u00cdA refers to a comprehensive collection of references and studies that support various guidelines and recommendations in the field of nutrition and clinical practice. It encompasses a wide range of topics, including methodologies and findings in nutritional assessment, as well as specific areas such as the use of parenteral and enteral nutrition in both adult and pediatric patients. The bibliography includes references related to the diagnosis and treatment of conditions like Adrenoleukodystrophy, inflammatory bowel disease, and hyponatremia. Additionally, it features studies that address the interactions between medications and nutrients, highlighting their relevance to clinical practice. The section serves as a vital resource, providing a list of sources that underpin the information presented in the document, thereby emphasizing the importance of nutrition in various health contexts, including neurological diseases and renal conditions."}{"title": "PERFORMANCE STATUS SCALE:The Performance Status Scale is designed to evaluate the disability related to eating and oral communication in head and neck cancer patients."}{"title": "FUNCTIONAL ORAL INTAKE SCALE:The Functional Oral Intake Scale is developed to document the functional level of oral intake of food and liquids in stroke patients, considering modifications in swallowing."}{"title": "DYSPHAGIA OUTCOME SEVERITY SCALE:The Dysphagia Outcome Severity Scale measures the functional level and severity of oropharyngeal dysphagia across various pathologies."}{"title": "LIST MA:List MA is one of the authors of the Performance Status Scale for head and neck cancer patients."}{"title": "O'NEIL KH:O'Neil KH is one of the authors of the Dysphagia Outcome and Severity Scale."}{"title": "CANCER:Cancer is a complex group of diseases characterized by the uncontrolled growth of abnormal cells in the body. This uncontrolled cell proliferation can lead to a variety of health complications, including cachexia, sarcopenia, malnutrition, diabetes, and hypercalcemia, particularly in older patients. Cancer significantly impacts the health and functional status of individuals, contributing to frailty and reducing overall resilience.\n\nThe disease can manifest in various parts of the body, including the head, neck, and thyroid gland, with specific types such as differentiated thyroid cancer being addressed in clinical guidelines. Cancer treatment often necessitates specialized nutritional support due to the effects of both the disease and its treatment on patients' ability to eat and maintain adequate nutrition. \n\nDietary and lifestyle factors play a crucial role in cancer risk, with studies indicating that habits such as the consumption of fruits and vegetables can influence susceptibility. Additionally, certain nutritional supplements, like arginine and glutamine, have been the focus of research regarding their potential benefits for cancer patients.\n\nOverall, cancer is a chronic condition that poses significant health challenges and requires complex treatment strategies, as well as tailored dietary guidelines to support affected individuals."}{"title": "FOOD INTAKE LEVEL SCALE:The Food Intake LEVEL Scale (FILS) is a tool developed to measure the severity of dysphagia by examining the degree to which patients consume food daily, particularly in palliative care settings."}{"title": "MD ANDERSON DYSPHAGIA INVENTORY:The MD Anderson Dysphagia Inventory (MDADI) is a dysphagia-specific quality-of-life questionnaire designed for patients with head and neck cancer, assessing the impact of dysphagia on their daily lives."}{"title": "KUNIEDA K:Kunieda K is one of the authors who contributed to the development of the Food Intake LEVEL Scale, focusing on measuring dysphagia severity."}{"title": "CHEN AY:Chen AY is one of the authors involved in the development and validation of the MD Anderson Dysphagia Inventory, which assesses the quality of life impact of dysphagia in cancer patients."}{"title": "NUTRITION:Nutrition is a comprehensive field of study and practice that focuses on the dietary needs and health impacts of food consumption. It encompasses the intake of food and nutrients, which are essential for maintaining health, growth, and disease management. Nutrition plays a critical role in various health contexts, including the prevention and management of diseases such as cancer, cardiovascular conditions, diabetes, and cognitive disorders like Alzheimer's and dementia.\n\nThe field addresses the dietary requirements of different populations, including infants, children, and patients with specific health conditions. For instance, nutrition is vital in managing inflammatory bowel disease, sarcopenia, frailty, and conditions like nephrolithiasis and gout. It is also crucial in the recovery process for patients undergoing preoperative and postoperative care, as well as in the management of eating disorders and during treatments like bone marrow transplantation and parenteral nutrition.\n\nResearch in nutrition includes studies on dietary practices, food allergies, and the effects of specific food groups, such as dairy products, on health. Journals dedicated to nutrition publish findings on nutritional assessment techniques, the role of nutrition in liver disease management, and the overall impact of dietary choices on health outcomes.\n\nOverall, nutrition is a vital aspect of health that influences not only physical well-being but also cognitive function and quality of life, highlighting the importance of proper dietary management across various medical contexts."}{"title": "DEGLUTION:Deglution is the act of swallowing, which is directly related to dysphagia and its assessment through various scales."}{"title": "CLINICAL STAFF:Clinical staff refers to healthcare professionals who administer dysphagia assessments and provide recommendations based on their findings."}{"title": "SCORE:The score in dysphagia assessments indicates the severity of the condition, influencing dietary recommendations and patient care."}{"title": "VIDEOFLUOROSCOPY:"}{"title": "SWALLOWING QUALITY OF LIFE QUESTIONNAIRE:The Swallowing Quality of Life Questionnaire (SWAL-QOL) is a tool used to measure the impact of oropharyngeal dysphagia on quality of life from the patient's perspective."}{"title": "SWAL-CARE:SWAL-CARE is an outcomes tool that evaluates the quality of care and patient satisfaction regarding oropharyngeal dysphagia treatment."}{"title": "DYSPHAGIA HANDICAP INDEX:The Dysphagia Handicap Index (DHI) measures the impact of dysphagia on quality of life across emotional, physical, and functional domains from the patient's perspective."}{"title": "SILBERGLEIT AK:Silbergleit AK is one of the authors who developed the Dysphagia Handicap Index."}{"title": "AUTOR/REFERENCIA:The term \"Autor/Referencia\" refers to the authors and references cited in the context of the SWAL-QOL and DHI tools, indicating the research background of these assessments."}{"title": "SWAL-QOL:"}{"title": "DEGLUTITION HANDICAP INDEX:The Deglutition Handicap Index is a self-assessment questionnaire designed to evaluate the quality of life in patients with swallowing disorders, focusing on physical, functional, and emotional aspects."}{"title": "WOISARD V:Woisard V is an author who contributed to the validation of the Deglutition Handicap Index and has published research on swallowing disorders."}{"title": "ANDRIEUX MP:Andrieux MP is an author who co-authored the validation study of the Deglutition Handicap Index."}{"title": "PUECH M:Puech M is an author involved in the research and validation of the Deglutition Handicap Index."}{"title": "MONTSE MART\u00cdNEZ LI\u00c9BANA:Montserrat Mart\u00ednez Li\u00e9bana is an author involved in the recipes for Cocina Hospitalaria."}{"title": "RECETAS DE LA COCINA HOSPITALARIA:The recipes of Cocina Hospitalaria refer to a collection of culinary instructions designed for hospital settings, focusing on patient nutrition."}{"title": "COLIFLOR CON BECHAMEL:A dish made with cauliflower and b\u00e9chamel sauce, prepared as part of a recipe for individuals with dysphagia."}{"title": "PUR\u00c9 DE GARBANZOS:A dish made from chickpeas, designed for individuals with dysphagia, featuring a specific preparation method."}{"title": "VERDURAS HERVIDAS CON CREMA DE GUISANTES:VERDURAS HERVIDAS CON CREMA DE GUISANTES is a dish that features boiled vegetables accompanied by a creamy pea sauce. This dish is specifically tailored for individuals with dysphagia, making it suitable for those who have difficulty swallowing. The recipe emphasizes the use of soft, easily digestible ingredients, ensuring that it meets the dietary needs of its intended audience."}{"title": "ACEITE DE OLIVA:Aceite de Oliva, or olive oil, is a versatile cooking oil widely used in various recipes, including those designed for dysphagia management. It is recognized for its health benefits, particularly its high content of oleic acid, a monounsaturated fatty acid associated with cardiovascular health. This oil is a staple in Mediterranean diets and is commonly used for frying, dressing dishes, and enhancing flavors in recipes such as Crema Fr\u00eda de Mel\u00f3n con Jam\u00f3n, Salmorejo, and Magdalena de espinacas.\n\nIn Spain, Aceite de Oliva can be classified under Denominaci\u00f3n de Origen Protegida (DOP), with over 30 designated regions producing this high-quality oil. It serves as a source of healthy fats and is recommended for balancing omega-3 and omega-6 fatty acids in dietary mixes. Additionally, olive oil is noted for its role in parenteral nutrition and is suggested for use in low-sodium cooking.\n\nOverall, Aceite de Oliva is not only a flavorful ingredient but also a key component of a healthy diet, contributing to lower blood pressure levels and promoting overall well-being, making it suitable for all age groups, including children."}{"title": "MEDALLONES DE MERLUZA EN SALSA VERDE:MEDALLONES DE MERLUZA EN SALSA VERDE is a dish that features hake medallions served in a flavorful green sauce. This dish is specifically designed for individuals with dysphagia, making it suitable for patients who experience swallowing difficulties. The preparation includes a detailed recipe that outlines the necessary ingredients and cooking methods to create this accessible and nutritious meal."}{"title": "RALLADURA DE HUEVO CON TOMATE:RALLADURA DE HUEVO CON TOMATE is a dish that combines grated egg with tomato, specifically designed for individuals with dysphagia, ensuring it is easy to swallow. The preparation involves using eggs and tomato sauce, complemented by steamed potatoes, which are boiled and mashed to create a smooth texture. This dish caters to dietary needs while providing a flavorful and nutritious option."}{"title": "LASA\u00d1A DE CALABAC\u00cdN Y RABO DE TORO:A dish made with zucchini and oxtail, tailored for individuals with dysphagia."}{"title": "DELICIAS DE AT\u00daN CON TOMATE:\"DELICIAS DE AT\u00daN CON TOMATE\" is a dish that features tuna loin, onion, leek, and tomato sauce, which is formed into various shapes and cooked in a rich tomato sauce. This dish is not only flavorful but also suitable for individuals with dysphagia, making it accessible for those who require softer food options."}{"title": "SUFL\u00c9 DE SALM\u00d3N EN SALSA DE NARANJA:\"SUFL\u00c9 DE SALM\u00d3N EN SALSA DE NARANJA\" is a culinary dish that features a souffl\u00e9 made from salmon, accompanied by a flavorful orange sauce. This dish is specifically designed for individuals with dysphagia, ensuring that it is both palatable and easy to consume for those who may have difficulty swallowing."}{"title": "MILHOJAS DE CALABAZA Y EMPERADOR:MILHOJAS DE CALABAZA Y EMPERADOR is a culinary dish that consists of layers of pumpkin and emperor fish. It is specifically designed for individuals with swallowing difficulties, including those with dysphagia. This dish caters to the dietary needs of those who may struggle with traditional food textures, ensuring a safe and enjoyable eating experience."}{"title": "NATILLAS DE HUEVO CASERAS:NATILLAS DE HUEVO CASERAS is a traditional homemade egg custard dessert that is made with egg yolks, milk, and sweeteners. This dessert is particularly suitable for individuals with dysphagia, making it a popular choice in hospital kitchens. Its creamy texture and rich flavor make it a comforting option for those who may have difficulty swallowing, while also retaining its status as a beloved classic in various culinary traditions."}{"title": "CREMA DE QUESO CON PUR\u00c9 DE MEMBRILLO:Crema de queso con pur\u00e9 de membrillo is a dessert that combines cheese cream and quince puree, specifically designed for individuals with dysphagia. This dish is prepared using fresh cheese, membrillo, and milk, which are mixed together and then refrigerated to achieve the desired consistency. The combination of these ingredients creates a creamy and flavorful treat that caters to those who may have difficulty swallowing, while also offering a delightful taste experience."}{"title": "MELOCOT\u00d3N CON QUESO:Melocot\u00f3n con queso is a dish that features peaches served with cheese, specifically designed for individuals with dysphagia, a condition that makes swallowing difficult. This dish is made from peaches in syrup paired with fresh cheese, and it is commonly prepared for patients in hospital settings, ensuring that it meets the dietary needs of those who may have difficulty consuming regular foods."}{"title": "MANZANA ASADA RELLENA DE CREMA DE LIM\u00d3N:The \"MANZANA ASADA RELLENA DE CREMA DE LIM\u00d3N\" is a dessert that features a baked apple filled with a creamy lemon filling. This dish is prepared using specific ingredients and culinary techniques, making it a delightful treat. It is also suitable for individuals with dysphagia, ensuring that it can be enjoyed by those who may have difficulty swallowing. Overall, the \"MANZANA ASADA RELLENA DE CREMA DE LIM\u00d3N\" combines the comforting texture of baked apple with the refreshing taste of lemon cream, making it a versatile and appealing dessert option."}{"title": "SEMIFR\u00cdO DE PI\u00d1A:The SEMIFR\u00cdO DE PI\u00d1A is a semi-frozen dessert specifically crafted for individuals with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. This dessert is made using pineapple, yogurt, and gelatin, ensuring it is both palatable and suitable for those with specific dietary needs. The combination of these ingredients creates a refreshing and smooth texture, making it an ideal choice for patients requiring modified food textures."}{"title": "PUDIN DE MELOCOT\u00d3N Y QUESO:PUDIN DE MELOCOT\u00d3N Y QUESO is a dessert recipe that combines the flavors of peach and cheese to create a unique pudding. The recipe includes detailed instructions on the ingredients and the cooking process, making it accessible for those looking to prepare this dish. Additionally, this pudding is specifically tailored for individuals with dysphagia, ensuring that it is suitable for those who may have difficulty swallowing. Overall, PUDIN DE MELOCOT\u00d3N Y QUESO is a delightful and accommodating dessert option that highlights the harmonious blend of peach and cheese."}{"title": "FLAN DE HUEVO CASERO:FLAN DE HUEVO CASERO is a homemade egg flan dessert designed to be suitable for individuals with dysphagia. This dessert is prepared using a recipe that includes key ingredients such as milk and sugar, ensuring it meets the dietary needs of those who may have difficulty swallowing."}{"title": "PERAS CON COULIS DE FRUTOS ROJOS:\"PERAS CON COULIS DE FRUTOS ROJOS\" is a dessert recipe that features pears served with a red fruit coulis. The dish includes detailed preparation steps and a list of ingredients necessary for its creation. Additionally, it is specifically designed to cater to individuals with dysphagia, ensuring that the texture and presentation are suitable for those who may have difficulty swallowing. This makes \"PERAS CON COULIS DE FRUTOS ROJOS\" not only a delicious dessert option but also an accessible one for people with dietary restrictions related to swallowing."}{"title": "CREMOSO DE MANZANA:CREMOSO DE MANZANA is a creamy apple dessert recipe designed specifically for individuals with dysphagia. This dessert incorporates yogurt and gelatin, making it both delicious and suitable for those who may have difficulty swallowing."}{"title": "FLAN DE CAF\u00c9:FLAN DE CAF\u00c9 is a coffee flan dessert specifically designed for individuals with dysphagia, ensuring it is suitable for those who have difficulty swallowing. This dessert is made with a combination of eggs, milk, sugar, and coffee, and is prepared by baking in a water bath. It is typically served with a layer of caramel, enhancing its flavor and presentation."}{"title": "HUESO DE TERNERA:An ingredient used in the preparation of various dishes, including those for dysphagia management."}{"title": "HUESO DE JAM\u00d3N:HUESO DE JAM\u00d3N refers to a ham bone that serves as an essential ingredient in the preparation of various dishes, particularly in recipes designed for dysphagia management. It is notably used for flavoring the broth in the traditional Menudillo de Cocido recipe, enhancing the overall taste and nutritional value of the dish."}{"title": "CARCASA DE POLLO:An ingredient used in the preparation of various dishes, including those for dysphagia management."}{"title": "LAUREL:Laurel, commonly known as bay leaf, is a versatile herb used for seasoning in a variety of culinary applications. It is particularly noted for its role in enhancing the flavor of dishes, including soups, stews, and sauces. Laurel is also utilized in specific recipes, such as hake medallions and gnocchi, where it contributes to the overall taste profile. Additionally, it is recognized for its use in managing dysphagia, as it can be incorporated into recipes designed for individuals with swallowing difficulties. Overall, laurel serves as a flavorful addition to many recipes, including those for boiled vegetables, making it a valuable herb in both everyday cooking and specialized dietary preparations."}{"title": "ENSALADILLA RUSA:A traditional Spanish salad recipe made with potatoes, carrots, tuna, and mayonnaise, suitable for dysphagia patients."}{"title": "SALMOREJO CON PERLITAS DE HUEVO:Salmorejo con perlitas de huevo is a cold Spanish tomato soup that is specifically designed to cater to dysphagia diets. This dish features a blend of ingredients including tomato, bread, and egg, and is typically served with egg pearls. It is often prepared in a hospital culinary context, highlighting its suitability for patients with dietary restrictions while still offering a flavorful and nutritious option."}{"title": "PATATA:Patata, commonly known as potato, is a starchy root vegetable that is widely utilized in cooking across various cuisines around the world. It is characterized by its versatility as an ingredient, appearing in numerous recipes such as Ralladura de huevo con tomate, Bacalao al cava, and Menudillo de Cocido, where it provides essential texture and substance. Patata is also a key component in dishes like gnocchi and is used to create pur\u00e9es, such as in the hake medallions recipe.\n\nIn terms of nutritional content, Patata contains a small amount of dietary fiber and has a low galactose content, measuring less than 5 mg per 100 g. The glycemic index of potatoes varies depending on the cooking method, with boiled potatoes having a high glycemic index of 121 and baked potatoes reaching 144. Overall, Patata is a significant food source that plays an important role in many culinary traditions, particularly for individuals with dysphagia, as it is featured in multiple recipes tailored for this condition."}{"title": "ZANAHORIA:Zanahoria, commonly known as carrot, is a versatile root vegetable celebrated for its sweetness, color, and nutritional value. It is frequently utilized in a variety of dishes, including sauces, soups, and salads, where it contributes both flavor and texture. Zanahoria is particularly noted for its role in dysphagia-friendly recipes, making it a suitable ingredient for individuals with swallowing difficulties. \n\nIn culinary applications, zanahoria is featured in traditional recipes such as Menudillo de Cocido and is an essential component in dishes like Milhojas de Calabaza y Emperador and hake medallions. It is also used in vegetable pies and as a base for purees, especially recommended during the semisolid diet phase following bariatric surgery.\n\nNutritionally, zanahoria is high in fiber and contains a moderate amount of galactose, ranging from 5-10 mg per 100 g. It has a low glycemic index of 23 when raw and a higher index of 70 when cooked, making it a healthy choice for various diets. Overall, zanahoria is a nutritious and flavorful vegetable that enhances a wide array of culinary creations."}{"title": "AT\u00daN EN ACEITE:Canned tuna in oil, used in the ensaladilla rusa recipe, providing protein and flavor."}{"title": "MAYONESA:Mayonesa, commonly known as mayonnaise, is a condiment made from emulsified egg yolks and oil. It is widely used in various recipes, including the traditional Spanish dish ensaladilla rusa. Depending on the recipe, mayonesa may contain lactose. However, it is important to note that mayonnaise is not permitted in modified diets. In culinary applications, mayonnaise is utilized in recipes such as cold salmon cake, where it contributes creaminess and flavor."}{"title": "HUEVO COCIDO:Boiled egg, an ingredient in the salmorejo recipe, providing protein and texture."}{"title": "CEBOLLA:Cebolla, commonly known as onion, is a bulb vegetable renowned for its strong flavor and aroma, making it an essential ingredient in a wide variety of culinary dishes. It is frequently saut\u00e9ed or cooked to enhance its natural sweetness, contributing significantly to the flavor profile of many recipes. Cebolla is utilized in the preparation of numerous dishes, including Crema Fr\u00eda de Mel\u00f3n con Jam\u00f3n, pur\u00e9 calabaza, pea sauce for boiled vegetables, cold salmon cake, hake medallions, vegetable pie, and gnocchi, among others.\n\nIn addition to its culinary uses, cebolla contains varying levels of fructans, which may affect individuals with FODMAP sensitivity. It also has a moderate amount of galactose, ranging between 5-10 mg per 100 grams. Overall, cebolla serves as a foundational ingredient in cooking, valued for its ability to enhance flavor and aroma across a diverse array of recipes."}{"title": "PUERRO:Puerro, commonly known as leek, is a vegetable that resembles an onion and is valued in cooking for its mild flavor. It is frequently used in the preparation of various culinary dishes, particularly soups and sauces, where it enhances the overall flavor profile. Puerro is an essential ingredient in several recipes, including pea sauce for boiled vegetables, hake medallions, and vegetable pie, showcasing its versatility in the kitchen. Additionally, it is a component in pur\u00e9 calabaza, further highlighting its culinary applications. However, it is important to note that puerro contains fructans, which may pose challenges for individuals with FODMAP intolerance. Overall, puerro is a flavorful and widely used vegetable in various cooking contexts."}{"title": "VINOBLANCO:White wine is an ingredient used in the preparation of the pea sauce for the boiled vegetables recipe."}{"title": "SAL:The entity \"SAL\" encompasses various aspects of salt, which is a mineral primarily composed of sodium and is a fundamental component in culinary practices and nutrition. Salt is widely recognized as the main source of sodium in the diet, commonly used for cooking and preserving food. It serves as a crucial seasoning that enhances the flavor of dishes, including those prepared in clinical settings, where it is utilized in hospital recipes to improve taste.\n\nHowever, the consumption of salt is a double-edged sword. While it is essential for health, its intake must be monitored and controlled according to the recommendations of the World Health Organization (WHO) to mitigate health risks. High salt consumption has been linked to cardiovascular mortality and other health conditions, including cancer. Therefore, it is advised that individuals limit their salt intake to promote better cardiovascular health.\n\nIn clinical nutrition, SAL also refers to the salts used in products that affect the solubility of proteins and other ingredients, highlighting its importance beyond mere seasoning. Overall, while salt is a ubiquitous and vital dietary component, its consumption should be approached with caution to avoid adverse health effects."}{"title": "PIMIENTA:Pimienta, commonly known as pepper, is a versatile spice used to enhance the flavor of various dishes. It serves as a seasoning in multiple recipes, including cold salmon cake and vegetable pie, allowing for flavor adjustment and improvement. As a key ingredient, pimienta contributes to the overall taste profile of these dishes, making it an essential component in culinary preparations."}{"title": "LA COCINA HOSPITALARIA:La Cocina Hospitalaria is an organization that provides recipes and culinary techniques for hospital settings, focusing on nutritional needs."}{"title": "MAGDALENA DE ESPINACAS:Magdalena de espinacas is a baked dish made with spinach and eggs, designed for patients with specific dietary requirements."}{"title": "CHUPITO DE CALABAC\u00cdN Y AT\u00daN:Chupito de calabac\u00edn y at\u00fan is a dish that involves zucchini filled with a mixture of tuna and tomato, suitable for hospital meals."}{"title": "PAN:PAN refers to bread and baked goods, which are included in various meals throughout the diet plan. It is an essential ingredient in Salmorejo, contributing to the soup's texture. While bread is permitted in modified diets, it may pose risks if it is hard or crusty. Additionally, individuals with phenylketonuria should consume bread with caution, as it may contain phenylalanine. Overall, PAN encompasses a variety of bread types that can be part of a diet, but careful consideration is necessary regarding their texture and potential dietary restrictions."}{"title": "HUEVO:Huevo, or egg, is a versatile ingredient widely used in various culinary recipes. It plays a crucial role in binding mixtures together, as seen in dishes like cold salmon cake and vegetable pie. Additionally, eggs are essential in cooking for binding ingredients in recipes such as croquetas. They are a common component in numerous dishes, including Ralladura de huevo con tomate, Salmorejo, and Magdalena de espinacas, contributing not only to the texture but also providing a valuable source of protein. Overall, huevo is an integral part of many recipes, enhancing both flavor and nutritional value."}{"title": "ESPINACAS:Espinacas, commonly known as spinach, are nutrient-rich leafy greens that provide 4 mg of iron per 100 grams. They are a versatile ingredient in various culinary applications, including dishes like Magdalena de espinacas and vegetable pies, where they contribute both flavor and nutritional value. Espinacas are particularly noted for their richness in several B vitamins, making them a beneficial addition to a balanced diet. However, it is important to note that spinach contains moderate levels of purines, which can influence uric acid levels in the body. This characteristic has led to studies examining the effects of spinach on uric acid levels, particularly for individuals with dietary restrictions or conditions such as dysphagia, where purees are often utilized. Overall, espinacas are celebrated for their health benefits and versatility in cooking."}{"title": "AT\u00daN:AT\u00daN, or tuna, is a type of fish that serves as a primary ingredient in various dishes, including Chupito de calabac\u00edn y at\u00fan, where it contributes both protein and flavor. Additionally, AT\u00daN is noted for its significant purine content, which can influence uric acid levels in the body."}{"title": "TOMATE:Tomate, also known as tomato, is a fruit that is widely utilized in cooking and is recognized for its juicy texture. It is commonly featured in salads, sauces, and a variety of dishes, making it a versatile ingredient in culinary practices. Tomate is not only a key component in specific recipes such as Ralladura de huevo con tomate and Delicias de at\u00fan con tomate, but it is also recommended as part of a balanced diet, particularly for children. Additionally, tomatoes are a source of dietary fiber and are frequently used as a base ingredient in numerous recipes, highlighting their importance in both nutrition and gastronomy."}{"title": "PASTEL DE VERDURAS:A vegetable pie recipe designed for individuals with dysphagia, including specific ingredients and cooking techniques."}{"title": "FLOR DE \u00d1OQUIS CON SALSA DE QUESOS:A gnocchi dish with cheese sauce, tailored for those with dysphagia, featuring detailed preparation steps."}{"title": "JUD\u00cdAS VERDES:Jud\u00edas Verdes, commonly known as green beans, are a type of vegetable that serves as a key ingredient in various recipes, including vegetable pie. These green beans are recognized for their dietary fiber content, making them a nutritious addition to meals. Additionally, jud\u00edas verdes are noted for their inclusion in a strict low-sodium diet, highlighting their versatility and health benefits in various culinary contexts."}{"title": "CALABAC\u00cdN:Calabac\u00edn, commonly known as zucchini, is a versatile summer squash celebrated for its mild flavor and nutritional benefits. It is a gluten-free vegetable that is featured in various dietary plans, making it suitable for those with gluten sensitivities. Calabac\u00edn contains a low amount of galactose, specifically less than 5 mg per 100 grams, which adds to its appeal for health-conscious individuals.\n\nThis vegetable is widely used in a variety of recipes, including lasagna, where it is often layered with meat and sauce, as well as in salads and vegetable pies. Its adaptability in cooking allows it to be incorporated into numerous dishes, enhancing both flavor and nutrition. Overall, Calabac\u00edn is a popular ingredient in many culinary applications, appreciated for its health benefits and culinary versatility."}{"title": "SALSA DE TOMATE:Salsa de Tomate, commonly known as tomato sauce, serves multiple culinary purposes across various dishes. It is a key ingredient in Br\u00f3coli con Salsa Aurora, where it enhances both the flavor and color of the dish. Additionally, Salsa de Tomate is utilized in a cold salmon cake recipe, contributing flavor and moisture to the dish. It is also beneficial for individuals with swallowing difficulties, as it can be used to moisten foods, making them easier to consume. Furthermore, Salsa de Tomate is incorporated into a vegetable pie recipe, showcasing its versatility in enhancing a variety of meals."}{"title": "SALSA BECHAMEL:B\u00e9chamel sauce used as a component in the vegetable pie recipe."}{"title": "NATA PARA COCINAR:Cooking cream used in the gnocchi sauce."}{"title": "SURTIDO DE QUESOS:Assorted cheeses used in the gnocchi sauce."}˙.1␀␀␀␀␀õ/1␀␀␀␀␀901␀␀␀␀␀÷01␀␀␀␀␀o11␀␀␀␀␀*21␀␀␀␀␀º21␀␀␀␀␀k31␀␀␀␀␀*41␀␀␀␀␀¬41␀␀␀␀␀s51␀␀␀␀␀!61␀␀␀␀␀ƒ61␀␀␀␀␀D71␀␀␀␀␀%<1␀␀␀␀␀∫<1␀␀␀␀␀L=1␀␀␀␀␀f=1␀␀␀␀␀Ò=1␀␀␀␀␀g>1␀␀␀␀␀Ÿ>1␀␀␀␀␀\?1␀␀␀␀␀√@1␀␀␀␀␀)A1␀␀␀␀␀ÑA1␀␀␀␀␀␀B1␀␀␀␀␀aB1␀␀␀␀␀…B1␀␀␀␀␀íD1␀␀␀␀␀ˆD1␀␀␀␀␀dE1␀␀␀␀␀»E1␀␀␀␀␀.F1␀␀␀␀␀àF1␀␀␀␀␀ÊF1␀␀␀␀␀HG1␀␀␀␀␀¥G1␀␀␀␀␀H1␀␀␀␀␀òH1␀␀␀␀␀≠J1␀␀␀␀␀DL1␀␀␀␀␀ÆL1␀␀␀␀␀2M1␀␀␀␀␀õM1␀␀␀␀␀N1␀␀␀␀␀qN1␀␀␀␀␀⁄N1␀␀␀␀␀CO1␀␀␀␀␀uO1␀␀␀␀␀P1␀␀␀␀␀ÎQ1␀␀␀␀␀sR1␀␀␀␀␀S1␀␀␀␀␀ÚS1␀␀␀␀␀úT1␀␀␀␀␀OU1␀␀␀␀␀˝U1␀␀␀␀␀≥V1␀␀␀␀␀ŒX1␀␀␀␀␀MY1␀␀␀␀␀…Y1␀␀␀␀␀/Z1␀␀␀␀␀àZ1␀␀␀␀␀[1␀␀␀␀␀x[1␀␀␀␀␀‰[1␀␀␀␀␀^\1␀␀␀␀␀È\1␀␀␀␀␀J]1␀␀␀␀␀≤]1␀␀␀␀␀&^1␀␀␀␀␀ä^1␀␀␀␀␀Ó^1␀␀␀␀␀]_1␀␀␀␀␀Ê_1␀␀␀␀␀S`1␀␀␀␀␀∆`1␀␀␀␀␀Ma1␀␀␀␀␀∑a1␀␀␀␀␀èc1␀␀␀␀␀c1␀␀␀␀␀]d1␀␀␀␀␀‡d1␀␀␀␀␀De1␀␀␀␀␀•e1␀␀␀␀␀˜e1␀␀␀␀␀Wf1␀␀␀␀␀©f1␀␀␀␀␀6g1␀␀␀␀␀äg1␀␀␀␀␀Úg1␀␀␀␀␀{h1␀␀␀␀␀√h1␀␀␀␀␀i1␀␀␀␀␀`i1␀␀␀␀␀∞i1␀␀␀␀␀␀j1␀␀␀␀␀Tj1␀␀␀␀␀¢j1␀␀␀␀␀j1␀␀␀␀␀^k1␀␀␀␀␀≤k1␀␀␀␀␀l1␀␀␀␀␀\l1␀␀␀␀␀≥l1␀␀␀␀␀ˇl1␀␀␀␀␀xm1␀␀␀␀␀ m1␀␀